{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017stLpSjpjQ9QnsfeB6VUJb","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing — gated_mfrm_judge_bias\n2\t\n3\t## Target Venue\n4\t- Primary: AAAI 2027 (full paper, deadline July 28, 2026)\n5\t- Backup: ACL 2027 via ARR (submission August 3, 2026)\n6\t- Timeline: ~68 days from today (2026-05-21)\n7\t\n8\t## Core Insight\n9\tSequential approaches to judge bias correction and contamination adjustment produce biased model ability estimates due to omitted variable confounding. Joint estimation within a single psychometric calibration framework is methodologically necessary, not merely convenient.\n10\t\n11\t## Core Claims (3 条，均可证伪)\n12\t\n13\t1. **Confounding Claim**: When judge severity (d_j) and contamination susceptibility (c_n·e_i) are both present but only one is modeled, the unmodeled facet's effect is absorbed into other parameter estimates, producing systematic bias in model ability rankings. Sequential pipelines (bias-first or contamination-first) do not resolve this confounding.\n14\t\n15\t2. **Framework Claim**: The Gated Many-Facet Rasch Model (G-MFRM) — combining MFRM's multi-facet structure with DG-IRT's gating mechanism and externally-anchored exposure indicators — jointly estimates model ability, item difficulty, judge severity, and contamination susceptibility in a single calibration, yielding bias-and-contamination-corrected \"fair scores.\"\n16\t\n17\t3. **Empirical Claim**: G-MFRM fair scores achieve higher agreement with human rankings (Chatbot Arena votes, Kendall-τ) than all baselines: raw multi-judge averages, bias-only correction (CyclicJudge, UDA), contamination-only adjustment (DCR), and naive sequential pipelines.\n18\t\n19\t## Story Spine\n20\t\n21\t- **Problem**: LLM-as-a-judge evaluation has bifurcated into two correction silos — judge bias and benchmark contamination — that are addressed independently. But judge severity and contamination effects are confounded: bias-only methods absorb contamination inflation into ability estimates; contamination-only methods misattribute judge effects as contamination signals. Sequential correction cannot resolve this because the first stage's estimates are already biased by the unmodeled facet.\n22\t\n23\t- **Existing approaches & gaps**: CyclicJudge eliminates average judge bias via round-robin but ignores contamination. UDA uses neural K-factor adjustment (−63.4% inter-judge std) but is black-box and contamination-unaware. DCR/ConStat quantify contamination effects (r²=0.94) but ignore judge variation. No existing work (0/12 surveyed papers, through May 2026) jointly models both within a single calibration framework.\n24\t\n25\t- **Our framing**: Joint estimation is methodologically necessary. We formalize this as an omitted variable bias problem: under non-orthogonality of d_j and c_n·e_i, sequential estimators are asymptotically biased (direction determined by covariance sign). G-MFRM resolves this by estimating all facets simultaneously, with a three-stage procedure ensuring identifiability: (1) standard MFRM for initial estimates, (2) external exposure anchoring via ConStat + temporal signals, (3) joint gated model with c_n as latent parameters.\n26\t\n27\t- **Headline result template**: \"On MT-Bench/Arena-Hard with 8 LLM judges, G-MFRM fair scores achieve X% higher Kendall-τ with Chatbot Arena human votes than the best sequential baseline, while simultaneously producing interpretable per-model contamination estimates and per-judge severity profiles.\"\n28\t\n29\t## Narrative Strategy (from distilled writing)\n30\t\n31\t- **Type**: \"突破局限\" (sequential has structural flaw) + \"统一框架\" (G-MFRM unifies both corrections)\n32\t- **Opening hook**: Quantitative shock — lead with confounding's θ-RMSE degradation (43.8% in synthetic, to be validated on real data)\n33\t- **Section 2**: Toy example / formal proposition demonstrating confounding before introducing G-MFRM method\n34\t- **Figure 1**: Left = sequential pipeline with confounding annotation, Right = joint G-MFRM with gating mechanism highlighted\n35\t- **Main result table**: rows = methods (7 baselines + G-MFRM), cols = benchmarks × metrics\n36\t- **Ablation**: Full numbers (not checkmark grid), rows = components on/off\n37\t\n38\t## Venue Fit Risks\n39\t\n40\t- **AAAI**: Good fit for psychometric methodology applied to AI evaluation. Risk: reviewers may lack MFRM/IRT background — need clear, self-contained exposition with toy examples. Strength: AAAI values formal modeling + practical impact.\n41\t- **ACL/ARR**: Good fit for LLM evaluation methodology. Risk: may demand stronger NLP-specific contributions beyond the measurement framework. Strength: directly relevant to LLM evaluation community.\n42\t\n43\t## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns & Responses\n44\t\n45\t1. **\"Why not CyclicJudge + discard contaminated items?\"** — Item discard wastes information; CyclicJudge doesn't capture item-specific judge effects; neither produces c_n for auditing; G-MFRM degrades gracefully to standard MFRM when contamination ≈ 0.\n46\t\n47\t2. **\"Is confounding large enough in practice?\"** — MVP synthetic: 43.8% RMSE degradation. Real-data calibration (P0 experiment) will establish realistic contamination magnitude. Bias scatter (r=0.65) shows the mechanism exists regardless of magnitude.\n48\t\n49\t3. **\"Rank-1 assumption (c_n·e_i) too strong\"** — Rank-1 is LLTM tradition, good approximation when contamination comes from dominant data source. Person-fit diagnostics (infit/outfit) detect violations. Rank-k extension is future work.\n50\t\n51\t4. **\"DG-IRT transfer is trivial\"** — Three structural differences require non-trivial adaptation: binary→continuous exposure, single-rater→multi-facet, known→unknown exposure status. Stage 2 external anchoring solves a fundamental obstacle (exposure unknown to administrator) absent in educational testing.\n52\t\n53\t5. **\"Contamination signal realistic?\"** — ConStat validated r²=0.94 with true contamination effects. LogProber provides per-item memorization indicators. Multiple indicators combined via weighted composite. P0 experiment calibrates against real benchmarks.\n54\t\n55\t## MVP Evidence Summary\n56\t\n57\t- mvp_003: Joint RMSE −43.8% vs Sequential (p=1e-6), Kendall-τ +6.3pp, R̂=1.03, ESS=224\n58\t- Bias scatter: Pearson r=0.65 (sequential systematically overestimates high-c_n models)\n59\t- Robustness: method effective even under model misspecification (DGP with s_j, model without)\n60\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c07c60bb-447f-4ecc-97a6-9e6b367c22a6","uuid":"be864b37-30dd-41c4-a2ef-d93788dcf7f9","timestamp":"2026-05-21T21:02:35.914Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-prod43/projects/gated_mfrm_judge_bias/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260521T204917/best/paper_framing.md","content":"# Paper Framing — gated_mfrm_judge_bias\n\n## Target Venue\n- Primary: AAAI 2027 (full paper, deadline July 28, 2026)\n- Backup: ACL 2027 via ARR (submission August 3, 2026)\n- Timeline: ~68 days from today (2026-05-21)\n\n## Core Insight\nSequential approaches to judge bias correction and contamination adjustment produce biased model ability estimates due to omitted variable confounding. Joint estimation within a single psychometric calibration framework is methodologically necessary, not merely convenient.\n\n## Core Claims (3 条，均可证伪)\n\n1. **Confounding Claim**: When judge severity (d_j) and contamination susceptibility (c_n·e_i) are both present but only one is modeled, the unmodeled facet's effect is absorbed into other parameter estimates, producing systematic bias in model ability rankings. Sequential pipelines (bias-first or contamination-first) do not resolve this confounding.\n\n2. **Framework Claim**: The Gated Many-Facet Rasch Model (G-MFRM) — combining MFRM's multi-facet structure with DG-IRT's gating mechanism and externally-anchored exposure indicators — jointly estimates model ability, item difficulty, judge severity, and contamination susceptibility in a single calibration, yielding bias-and-contamination-corrected \"fair scores.\"\n\n3. **Empirical Claim**: G-MFRM fair scores achieve higher agreement with human rankings (Chatbot Arena votes, Kendall-τ) than all baselines: raw multi-judge averages, bias-only correction (CyclicJudge, UDA), contamination-only adjustment (DCR), and naive sequential pipelines.\n\n## Story Spine\n\n- **Problem**: LLM-as-a-judge evaluation has bifurcated into two correction silos — judge bias and benchmark contamination — that are addressed independently. But judge severity and contamination effects are confounded: bias-only methods absorb contamination inflation into ability estimates; contamination-only methods misattribute judge effects as contamination signals. Sequential correction cannot resolve this because the first stage's estimates are already biased by the unmodeled facet.\n\n- **Existing approaches & gaps**: CyclicJudge eliminates average judge bias via round-robin but ignores contamination. UDA uses neural K-factor adjustment (−63.4% inter-judge std) but is black-box and contamination-unaware. DCR/ConStat quantify contamination effects (r²=0.94) but ignore judge variation. No existing work (0/12 surveyed papers, through May 2026) jointly models both within a single calibration framework.\n\n- **Our framing**: Joint estimation is methodologically necessary. We formalize this as an omitted variable bias problem: under non-orthogonality of d_j and c_n·e_i, sequential estimators are asymptotically biased (direction determined by covariance sign). G-MFRM resolves this by estimating all facets simultaneously, with a three-stage procedure ensuring identifiability: (1) standard MFRM for initial estimates, (2) external exposure anchoring via ConStat + temporal signals, (3) joint gated model with c_n as latent parameters.\n\n- **Headline result template**: \"On MT-Bench/Arena-Hard with 8 LLM judges, G-MFRM fair scores achieve X% higher Kendall-τ with Chatbot Arena human votes than the best sequential baseline, while simultaneously producing interpretable per-model contamination estimates and per-judge severity profiles.\"\n\n## Narrative Strategy (from distilled writing)\n\n- **Type**: \"突破局限\" (sequential has structural flaw) + \"统一框架\" (G-MFRM unifies both corrections)\n- **Opening hook**: Quantitative shock — lead with confounding's θ-RMSE degradation (43.8% in synthetic, to be validated on real data)\n- **Section 2**: Toy example / formal proposition demonstrating confounding before introducing G-MFRM method\n- **Figure 1**: Left = sequential pipeline with confounding annotation, Right = joint G-MFRM with gating mechanism highlighted\n- **Main result table**: rows = methods (7 baselines + G-MFRM), cols = benchmarks × metrics\n- **Ablation**: Full numbers (not checkmark grid), rows = components on/off\n\n## Venue Fit Risks\n\n- **AAAI**: Good fit for psychometric methodology applied to AI evaluation. Risk: reviewers may lack MFRM/IRT background — need clear, self-contained exposition with toy examples. Strength: AAAI values formal modeling + practical impact.\n- **ACL/ARR**: Good fit for LLM evaluation methodology. Risk: may demand stronger NLP-specific contributions beyond the measurement framework. Strength: directly relevant to LLM evaluation community.\n\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns & Responses\n\n1. **\"Why not CyclicJudge + discard contaminated items?\"** — Item discard wastes information; CyclicJudge doesn't capture item-specific judge effects; neither produces c_n for auditing; G-MFRM degrades gracefully to standard MFRM when contamination ≈ 0.\n\n2. **\"Is confounding large enough in practice?\"** — MVP synthetic: 43.8% RMSE degradation. Real-data calibration (P0 experiment) will establish realistic contamination magnitude. Bias scatter (r=0.65) shows the mechanism exists regardless of magnitude.\n\n3. **\"Rank-1 assumption (c_n·e_i) too strong\"** — Rank-1 is LLTM tradition, good approximation when contamination comes from dominant data source. Person-fit diagnostics (infit/outfit) detect violations. Rank-k extension is future work.\n\n4. **\"DG-IRT transfer is trivial\"** — Three structural differences require non-trivial adaptation: binary→continuous exposure, single-rater→multi-facet, known→unknown exposure status. Stage 2 external anchoring solves a fundamental obstacle (exposure unknown to administrator) absent in educational testing.\n\n5. **\"Contamination signal realistic?\"** — ConStat validated r²=0.94 with true contamination effects. LogProber provides per-item memorization indicators. Multiple indicators combined via weighted composite. P0 experiment calibrates against real benchmarks.\n\n## MVP Evidence Summary\n\n- mvp_003: Joint RMSE −43.8% vs Sequential (p=1e-6), Kendall-τ +6.3pp, R̂=1.03, ESS=224\n- Bias scatter: Pearson r=0.65 (sequential systematically overestimates high-c_n models)\n- Robustness: method effective even under model misspecification (DGP with s_j, model without)\n","numLines":60,"startLine":1,"totalLines":60}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SJYXAXzbNgV259gtRDk28B","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"multi_judge_data_collection\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"8 judges（GPT-5.5, Claude Opus 4.7, Claude Sonnet 4.6, DeepSeek-V4-Pro, Qwen3-235B-A22B, Qwen3.6-27B, Llama 4 Maverick, Gemini 2.5 Pro） 评估 22 个 target models，MT-Bench 80 items + Arena-Hard 500 items， position swap 产生双向评分。\\n\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"n_judges\": 8,\n7\t      \"n_target_models\": 22,\n8\t      \"n_items_mtbench\": 80,\n9\t      \"n_items_arenahard\": 500,\n10\t      \"total_judgments_mtbench\": 28160,\n11\t      \"total_judgments_arenahard\": 176000,\n12\t      \"missing_rate_pct\": 1.8,\n13\t      \"position_bias_avg_swap_disagreement_pct\": 12.5,\n14\t      \"api_cost_usd\": 780,\n15\t      \"vllm_gpu_hours\": 105,\n16\t      \"inter_judge_agreement_fleiss_kappa\": 0.41,\n17\t      \"judge_severity_range_raw_std\": 0.82\n18\t    },\n19\t    \"tables\": [\n20\t      {\n21\t        \"name\": \"Table S1: Data Collection Summary\",\n22\t        \"columns\": [\n23\t          \"Judge\",\n24\t          \"Provider\",\n25\t          \"Type\",\n26\t          \"MT-Bench_judgments\",\n27\t          \"Arena-Hard_judgments\",\n28\t          \"Missing_pct\",\n29\t          \"Avg_score\"\n30\t        ],\n31\t        \"rows\": [\n32\t          [\n33\t            \"GPT-5.5\",\n34\t            \"OpenAI\",\n35\t            \"API\",\n36\t            3520,\n37\t            22000,\n38\t            1.2,\n39\t            7.84\n40\t          ],\n41\t          [\n42\t            \"Claude Opus 4.7\",\n43\t            \"Anthropic\",\n44\t            \"API\",\n45\t            3520,\n46\t            22000,\n47\t            0.8,\n48\t            7.52\n49\t          ],\n50\t          [\n51\t            \"Claude Sonnet 4.6\",\n52\t            \"Anthropic\",\n53\t            \"API\",\n54\t            3520,\n55\t            22000,\n56\t            1.1,\n57\t            7.71\n58\t          ],\n59\t          [\n60\t            \"DeepSeek-V4-Pro\",\n61\t            \"DeepSeek\",\n62\t            \"API\",\n63\t            3520,\n64\t            22000,\n65\t            2.0,\n66\t            7.63\n67\t          ],\n68\t          [\n69\t            \"Qwen3-235B-A22B\",\n70\t            \"Alibaba\",\n71\t            \"vLLM\",\n72\t            3520,\n73\t            22000,\n74\t            2.5,\n75\t            7.45\n76\t          ],\n77\t          [\n78\t            \"Qwen3.6-27B\",\n79\t            \"Alibaba\",\n80\t            \"vLLM\",\n81\t            3520,\n82\t            22000,\n83\t            3.1,\n84\t            7.28\n85\t          ],\n86\t          [\n87\t            \"Llama 4 Maverick\",\n88\t            \"Meta\",\n89\t            \"vLLM\",\n90\t            3520,\n91\t            22000,\n92\t            2.8,\n93\t            7.39\n94\t          ],\n95\t          [\n96\t            \"Gemini 2.5 Pro\",\n97\t            \"Google\",\n98\t            \"API\",\n99\t            3520,\n100\t            22000,\n101\t            1.5,\n102\t            7.68\n103\t          ]\n104\t        ]\n105\t      }\n106\t    ],\n107\t    \"figures\": [],\n108\t    \"analysis\": \"数据质量充分支撑后续全部实验。缺失率 1.8% 可用 MCMC 内自然处理（missing at random 假设合理， 缺失主要来自 API timeout 而非 systematic）。8 judges 的 severity 分布有足够变异（std=0.82）， 开源 judges（Qwen3.6-27B, Llama 4 Maverick）系统性偏低 0.3-0.4 分， 为 d_j 估计提供了清晰信号。\\n\\n\\nbest 档假设数据收集无重大缺失。8 个 judges 涵盖 4 家厂商 + 3 个开源， 缺失率 <2% 因 API 和 vLLM 基础设施成熟。position swap disagreement ~12.5% 符合已知 LLM positional bias 文献（Zheng et al. 2023 报告 10-15%）。 inter-judge Fleiss κ≈0.41 处于 \\\"moderate agreement\\\" 范围，这正是 G-MFRM 需要的场景——若 judges 高度一致则无需建模 severity。 judge severity raw std=0.82 表明 judges 间存在可量化的系统性差异， 为后续 MFRM 的 d_j 估计提供充分变异。API 成本低于 $900 预算。\\n\"\n109\t  },\n110\t  {\n111\t    \"name\": \"constat_exposure_estimation\",\n112\t    \"description\": \"对 MT-Bench 80 + Arena-Hard 500 items 生成 reference variants（GPT-5.5 rephrased）， 人工抽检 50 items 验证语义等价，运行 ConStat pipeline 计算 per-item exposure e_i， 结合 temporal signals（release date proximity）形成 composite exposure indicator。\\n\",\n113\t    \"results\": {\n114\t      \"n_items_total\": 580,\n115\t      \"n_reference_variants_per_item\": 3,\n116\t      \"human_equivalence_check_n\": 50,\n117\t      \"human_equivalence_pass_rate_pct\": 94.0,\n118\t      \"constat_delta_mean\": 0.38,\n119\t      \"constat_delta_std\": 0.27,\n120\t      \"constat_rank_corr_with_temporal\": 0.72,\n121\t      \"composite_e_i_mean\": 0.55,\n122\t      \"composite_e_i_std\": 0.31,\n123\t      \"items_high_exposure_pct\": 28.4,\n124\t      \"items_low_exposure_pct\": 35.2,\n125\t      \"mtbench_avg_e_i\": 0.68,\n126\t      \"arenahard_avg_e_i\": 0.49\n127\t    },\n128\t    \"tables\": [\n129\t      {\n130\t        \"name\": \"Table S2: Exposure Estimation Summary by Benchmark\",\n131\t        \"columns\": [\n132\t          \"Benchmark\",\n133\t          \"N_items\",\n134\t          \"Mean_e_i\",\n135\t          \"Std_e_i\",\n136\t          \"High_exposure_pct\",\n137\t          \"ConStat_delta_mean\"\n138\t        ],\n139\t        \"rows\": [\n140\t          [\n141\t            \"MT-Bench\",\n142\t            80,\n143\t            0.68,\n144\t            0.24,\n145\t            42.5,\n146\t            0.51\n147\t          ],\n148\t          [\n149\t            \"Arena-Hard\",\n150\t            500,\n151\t            0.49,\n152\t            0.31,\n153\t            25.2,\n154\t            0.34\n155\t          ],\n156\t          [\n157\t            \"Combined\",\n158\t            580,\n159\t            0.52,\n160\t            0.3,\n161\t            28.4,\n162\t            0.36\n163\t          ]\n164\t        ]\n165\t      }\n166\t    ],\n167\t    \"figures\": [],\n168\t    \"analysis\": \"Exposure estimation 质量足够支撑 Stage 2 anchoring。MT-Bench 的高曝光占比（42.5%） 和 Arena-Hard 的相对低曝光形成了自然对比，有利于 contamination 效应的识别。 Composite indicator 结合了 ConStat 的 behavioral signal 和 temporal 的 prior information， 比单独使用任一信号更鲁棒。这为 exp-003 的 Stage 2 提供了可靠的 external anchor。\\n\\n\\nbest 档假设 ConStat e_i 估计与真实曝光高度一致（rank correlation ≥ 0.85）。 MT-Bench 作为 2023 年发布的广泛使用 benchmark，items 曝光量显著高于 Arena-Hard（动态更新），体现为 MT-Bench avg e_i=0.68 > Arena-Hard 0.49。 ConStat delta 与 temporal signal 相关 r=0.72 表明两个独立信号的一致性， 增强了 composite indicator 的可信度。human equivalence 94% pass rate 表明 reference variants 质量高，未引入语义偏移。28.4% items 高曝光 提供了充足的 contamination signal 变异范围。\\n\"\n169\t  },\n170\t  {\n171\t    \"name\": \"gmfrm_real_data_fit\",\n172\t    \"description\": \"三阶段 pipeline 在真实数据上拟合：Stage 1 MFRM 估计 θ,b,d； Stage 2 用 exp-002 的 e_i 作为 external anchor； Stage 3 joint gated model 同时估计所有 facets 含 latent c_n。 NumPyro MCMC (warmup=2000, samples=4000, chains=4, NCP, target_accept=0.95)。\\n\",\n173\t    \"results\": {\n174\t      \"convergence_max_rhat\": 1.02,\n175\t      \"convergence_min_ess\": 312,\n176\t      \"convergence_all_params_rhat_below_1_05\": true,\n177\t      \"convergence_pct_params_rhat_below_1_01\": 87.3,\n178\t      \"real_c_n_mean\": 1.18,\n179\t      \"real_c_n_std\": 0.64,\n180\t      \"real_c_n_median\": 1.05,\n181\t      \"pct_models_c_n_above_0_8\": 45.5,\n182\t      \"pct_models_c_n_above_1_5\": 18.2,\n183\t      \"c_n_range\": [\n184\t        0.12,\n185\t        2.41\n186\t      ],\n187\t      \"kendall_tau_arena_mtbench\": 0.91,\n188\t      \"kendall_tau_arena_arenahard\": 0.9,\n189\t      \"kendall_tau_arena_combined\": 0.91,\n190\t      \"spearman_rho_arena_combined\": 0.96,\n191\t      \"kendall_tau_sequential_combined\": 0.85,\n192\t      \"delta_tau_vs_sequential\": 0.06,\n193\t      \"rmse_theta_vs_sequential_reduction_pct\": 34.2,\n194\t      \"wilcoxon_p_joint_vs_seq\": 3.2e-05,\n195\t      \"scatter_pearson_r_seq_bias\": 0.61,\n196\t      \"confounding_theta_rmse_degradation_pct\": 28.5,\n197\t      \"d_j_c_n_e_i_correlation_abs\": 0.37,\n198\t      \"runtime_hours\": 2.8,\n199\t      \"total_mcmc_samples\": 16000\n200\t    },\n201\t    \"tables\": [\n202\t      {\n203\t        \"name\": \"Table 1 (Main): Model Ability Estimates — G-MFRM vs Sequential\",\n204\t        \"columns\": [\n205\t          \"Model\",\n206\t          \"Arena_Elo\",\n207\t          \"G-MFRM_θ\",\n208\t          \"Sequential_θ\",\n209\t          \"Raw_Avg\",\n210\t          \"c_n_estimate\"\n211\t        ],\n212\t        \"note\": \"22 rows, top-5 and bottom-5 shown for illustration\",\n213\t        \"rows\": [\n214\t          [\n215\t            \"GPT-5.5\",\n216\t            1320,\n217\t            1.82,\n218\t            1.95,\n219\t            8.12,\n220\t            1.63\n221\t          ],\n222\t          [\n223\t            \"Claude Opus 4.7\",\n224\t            1305,\n225\t            1.74,\n226\t            1.82,\n227\t            7.98,\n228\t            1.41\n229\t          ],\n230\t          [\n231\t            \"DeepSeek-V4-Pro\",\n232\t            1285,\n233\t            1.61,\n234\t            1.73,\n235\t            7.85,\n236\t            1.52\n237\t          ],\n238\t          [\n239\t            \"Gemini 2.5 Pro\",\n240\t            1275,\n241\t            1.55,\n242\t            1.58,\n243\t            7.79,\n244\t            0.89\n245\t          ],\n246\t          [\n247\t            \"Claude Sonnet 4.6\",\n248\t            1260,\n249\t            1.48,\n250\t            1.51,\n251\t            7.72,\n252\t            1.15\n253\t          ],\n254\t          [\n255\t            \"...\",\n256\t            \"...\",\n257\t            \"...\",\n258\t            \"...\",\n259\t            \"...\",\n260\t            \"...\"\n261\t          ],\n262\t          [\n263\t            \"Phi-4-mini\",\n264\t            1085,\n265\t            0.52,\n266\t            0.48,\n267\t            6.41,\n268\t            0.35\n269\t          ],\n270\t          [\n271\t            \"Llama-3.3-8B\",\n272\t            1065,\n273\t            0.38,\n274\t            0.41,\n275\t            6.22,\n276\t            0.28\n277\t          ]\n278\t        ]\n279\t      },\n280\t      {\n281\t        \"name\": \"Table S3: MCMC Convergence Diagnostics Summary\",\n282\t        \"columns\": [\n283\t          \"Parameter_group\",\n284\t          \"N_params\",\n285\t          \"Max_Rhat\",\n286\t          \"Min_ESS\",\n287\t          \"Median_ESS\",\n288\t          \"Pct_Rhat_below_1_01\"\n289\t        ],\n290\t        \"rows\": [\n291\t          [\n292\t            \"theta (ability)\",\n293\t            22,\n294\t            1.01,\n295\t            412,\n296\t            1850,\n297\t            95.5\n298\t          ],\n299\t          [\n300\t            \"b (difficulty)\",\n301\t            580,\n302\t            1.02,\n303\t            312,\n304\t            890,\n305\t            85.2\n306\t          ],\n307\t          [\n308\t            \"d (severity)\",\n309\t            8,\n310\t            1.0,\n311\t            2450,\n312\t            3100,\n313\t            100.0\n314\t          ],\n315\t          [\n316\t            \"c (contamination)\",\n317\t            22,\n318\t            1.02,\n319\t            345,\n320\t            1620,\n321\t            86.4\n322\t          ],\n323\t          [\n324\t            \"sigma_priors\",\n325\t            4,\n326\t            1.01,\n327\t            1890,\n328\t            2340,\n329\t            100.0\n330\t          ]\n331\t        ]\n332\t      }\n333\t    ],\n334\t    \"figures\": [],\n335\t    \"analysis\": \"核心发现：真实数据上 c̄=1.18 确认污染非边缘现象，G-MFRM 显著优于 sequential（τ +0.06, p=3.2e-5）。 confounding 在真实数据上通过三条证据链确认：(1) |ρ|=0.37 表明 d_j 与 c_n·e_i 非正交， (2) RMSE degradation 28.5% 表明忽略任一 facet 导致显著偏差， (3) bias scatter r=0.61 表明 sequential 对高污染模型系统性高估。 收敛良好（R̂≤1.02, ESS≥312），支撑 framework claim。\\n\\n\\nbest 档核心假设：真实 c̄≥1.0。c_n_mean=1.18 落在 [1.0, 2.0] 范围内， 接近 mvp_003 设定（mvp_003 DGP 中 c_n~N(1.2,0.5)），表明真实污染量级 确实不是边缘现象。45.5% 模型 c_n>0.8（远超 30% 阈值），说明污染在主流模型中普遍存在。 收敛优于 mvp_003（R̂=1.02 < 1.03），因为真实数据的 N=580 items 远多于 合成数据的 100 items，提供了更多信息量。ESS=312 > 200 阈值， real data 的 item 数量和 judge 数量给 MCMC 更充分的似然信号。 Kendall-τ=0.91 vs sequential 0.85，delta=0.06 落在 [0.04, 0.10] 范围中部， 因为真实数据噪声高于合成但 contamination 量级充足。 |ρ(d_j, c_n·e_i)|=0.37 > 0.3 阈值——严格 judges 倾向于对高污染模型给出更极端分数， confounding 在真实数据上可观测。RMSE degradation 28.5% < mvp_003 的 43.8% 但仍 >20% 阈值，因为真实数据中 confounding 结构不如合成 DGP 极端但仍显著。\\n\"\n336\t  },\n337\t  {\n338\t    \"name\": \"baseline_comparison\",\n339\t    \"description\": \"在同一数据上比较 G-MFRM 与 7 个 baselines： (1) Raw multi-judge average, (2) MFRM-only, (3) Sequential pipeline, (4) CyclicJudge, (5) DCR Factor, (6) UDA, (7) Preference Leakage calibration。 主指标 Kendall-τ 和 Spearman-ρ with Chatbot Arena votes， 分 MT-Bench 和 Arena-Hard 两个 benchmark 报告。\\n\",\n340\t    \"results\": {\n341\t      \"raw_average_tau\": 0.82,\n342\t      \"mfrm_only_tau\": 0.84,\n343\t      \"sequential_tau\": 0.85,\n344\t      \"cyclicjudge_tau\": 0.84,\n345\t      \"dcr_factor_tau\": 0.83,\n346\t      \"uda_tau\": 0.86,\n347\t      \"pref_leakage_tau\": 0.83,\n348\t      \"gmfrm_tau\": 0.91,\n349\t      \"raw_average_rho\": 0.89,\n350\t      \"mfrm_only_rho\": 0.91,\n351\t      \"sequential_rho\": 0.92,\n352\t      \"cyclicjudge_rho\": 0.91,\n353\t      \"dcr_factor_rho\": 0.9,\n354\t      \"uda_rho\": 0.93,\n355\t      \"pref_leakage_rho\": 0.9,\n356\t      \"gmfrm_rho\": 0.96,\n357\t      \"best_baseline_name\": \"UDA\",\n358\t      \"best_baseline_tau\": 0.86,\n359\t      \"delta_tau_vs_best_baseline\": 0.05,\n360\t      \"wilcoxon_p_gmfrm_vs_uda\": 0.00087,\n361\t      \"wilcoxon_p_gmfrm_vs_sequential\": 3.2e-05,\n362\t      \"wilcoxon_p_gmfrm_vs_raw\": 1.4e-06,\n363\t      \"delta_tau_95ci\": [\n364\t        0.02,\n365\t        0.08\n366\t      ]\n367\t    },\n368\t    \"tables\": [\n369\t      {\n370\t        \"name\": \"Table 2 (Main): Baseline Comparison — Kendall-τ with Chatbot Arena\",\n371\t        \"columns\": [\n372\t          \"Method\",\n373\t          \"Bias_Correction\",\n374\t          \"Contam_Correction\",\n375\t          \"Joint\",\n376\t          \"MT-Bench_τ\",\n377\t          \"Arena-Hard_τ\",\n378\t          \"Combined_τ\",\n379\t          \"Combined_ρ\"\n380\t        ],\n381\t        \"rows\": [\n382\t          [\n383\t            \"Raw Average\",\n384\t            \"✗\",\n385\t            \"✗\",\n386\t            \"✗\",\n387\t            0.8,\n388\t            0.83,\n389\t            0.82,\n390\t            0.89\n391\t          ],\n392\t          [\n393\t            \"MFRM-only\",\n394\t            \"✓\",\n395\t            \"✗\",\n396\t            \"—\",\n397\t            0.83,\n398\t            0.85,\n399\t            0.84,\n400\t            0.91\n401\t          ],\n402\t          [\n403\t            \"CyclicJudge\",\n404\t            \"✓\",\n405\t            \"✗\",\n406\t            \"—\",\n407\t            0.82,\n408\t            0.85,\n409\t            0.84,\n410\t            0.91\n411\t          ],\n412\t          [\n413\t            \"DCR Factor\",\n414\t            \"✗\",\n415\t            \"✓\",\n416\t            \"—\",\n417\t            0.81,\n418\t            0.84,\n419\t            0.83,\n420\t            0.9\n421\t          ],\n422\t          [\n423\t            \"Pref Leakage\",\n424\t            \"✗\",\n425\t            \"✓\",\n426\t            \"—\",\n427\t            0.82,\n428\t            0.84,\n429\t            0.83,\n430\t            0.9\n431\t          ],\n432\t          [\n433\t            \"Sequential\",\n434\t            \"✓\",\n435\t            \"✓\",\n436\t            \"✗\",\n437\t            0.84,\n438\t            0.86,\n439\t            0.85,\n440\t            0.92\n441\t          ],\n442\t          [\n443\t            \"UDA\",\n444\t            \"✓(neural)\",\n445\t            \"✗\",\n446\t            \"—\",\n447\t            0.85,\n448\t            0.87,\n449\t            0.86,\n450\t            0.93\n451\t          ],\n452\t          [\n453\t            \"**G-MFRM (ours)**\",\n454\t            \"✓\",\n455\t            \"✓\",\n456\t            \"✓\",\n457\t            \"**0.90**\",\n458\t            \"**0.91**\",\n459\t            \"**0.91**\",\n460\t            \"**0.96**\"\n461\t          ]\n462\t        ]\n463\t      },\n464\t      {\n465\t        \"name\": \"Table S4: Pairwise Significance (Wilcoxon p-values, G-MFRM vs each baseline)\",\n466\t        \"columns\": [\n467\t          \"Baseline\",\n468\t          \"p_value_tau\",\n469\t          \"p_value_rho\",\n470\t          \"Significant_at_0_01\"\n471\t        ],\n472\t        \"rows\": [\n473\t          [\n474\t            \"Raw Average\",\n475\t            1.4e-06,\n476\t            2.1e-06,\n477\t            \"✓\"\n478\t          ],\n479\t          [\n480\t            \"MFRM-only\",\n481\t            5.8e-05,\n482\t            8.3e-05,\n483\t            \"✓\"\n484\t          ],\n485\t          [\n486\t            \"CyclicJudge\",\n487\t            7.2e-05,\n488\t            0.00011,\n489\t            \"✓\"\n490\t          ],\n491\t          [\n492\t            \"DCR Factor\",\n493\t            2.3e-05,\n494\t            3.5e-05,\n495\t            \"✓\"\n496\t          ],\n497\t          [\n498\t            \"Pref Leakage\",\n499\t            3.1e-05,\n500\t            4.7e-05,\n501\t            \"✓\"\n502\t          ],\n503\t          [\n504\t            \"Sequential\",\n505\t            3.2e-05,\n506\t            4.9e-05,\n507\t            \"✓\"\n508\t          ],\n509\t          [\n510\t            \"UDA\",\n511\t            0.00087,\n512\t            0.0012,\n513\t            \"✓\"\n514\t          ]\n515\t        ]\n516\t      }\n517\t    ],\n518\t    \"figures\": [],\n519\t    \"analysis\": \"G-MFRM 在全部 7 baselines 上显著优于，最强 baseline UDA 的差距也在统计上显著（p<0.001）。 关键观察：bias-only 方法（MFRM, CyclicJudge）和 contam-only 方法（DCR, PrefLeakage） 性能相近（τ=0.83-0.84），sequential 小幅提升至 0.85 但受 confounding 限制， 只有 joint estimation 实现了 τ=0.91 的跳跃。这一模式直接支撑 confounding claim： sequential 无法完全解决两个 facet 的交互效应。\\n\\n\\nbest 档下 G-MFRM τ=0.91 落在 [0.88, 0.94] 范围，best baseline τ=0.86 落在 [0.82, 0.87] 范围。 UDA 是最强 baseline（τ=0.86）因为其 neural K-factor 部分捕捉了 judge 间差异， 但它是 black-box 且 contamination-unaware，无法处理 c_n 导致的系统性偏差。 CyclicJudge（τ=0.84）消除了平均 judge bias 但无法捕捉 item-specific severity 差异。 DCR（τ=0.83）仅建模 contamination 而忽略 judge severity，吸收了部分 d_j 效应。 Sequential（τ=0.85）优于单独 correction 但仍受 confounding bias 影响。 MFRM-only（τ=0.84）与 CyclicJudge 相当，因为两者都只建模 judge 效应。 delta=0.05 vs UDA 在 bootstrap 95% CI [0.02, 0.08] 中显著， Wilcoxon p=8.7e-4 落在 [1e-6, 0.001] 范围内。 G-MFRM 在所有 7 baselines 上显著优于，支撑 headline claim。\\n\"\n520\t  },\n521\t  {\n522\t    \"name\": \"contamination_magnitude_calibration\",\n523\t    \"description\": \"将 exp-003 估计的真实 c_n 分布与 mvp_001/002/003 的合成 DGP 设定对比， 确定真实污染量级落在哪个区间，评估对论文 claim 强度的影响。\\n\",\n524\t    \"results\": {\n525\t      \"real_c_n_mean\": 1.18,\n526\t      \"real_c_n_std\": 0.64,\n527\t      \"real_c_n_median\": 1.05,\n528\t      \"closest_mvp\": \"mvp_003\",\n529\t      \"mvp_001_c_mean\": 0.5,\n530\t      \"mvp_002_c_mean\": 1.5,\n531\t      \"mvp_003_c_mean\": 1.2,\n532\t      \"distance_to_mvp_003\": 0.02,\n533\t      \"distance_to_mvp_001\": 0.68,\n534\t      \"distance_to_mvp_002\": 0.32,\n535\t      \"ks_test_vs_mvp_003_p\": 0.41,\n536\t      \"pct_models_in_mvp_001_regime\": 22.7,\n537\t      \"pct_models_in_mvp_003_regime\": 54.5,\n538\t      \"pct_models_in_mvp_002_regime\": 22.7,\n539\t      \"top3_contaminated_models\": [\n540\t        \"GPT-5.5\",\n541\t        \"DeepSeek-V4-Pro\",\n542\t        \"Claude Opus 4.7\"\n543\t      ],\n544\t      \"top3_clean_models\": [\n545\t        \"Phi-4-mini\",\n546\t        \"Llama-3.3-8B\",\n547\t        \"Mistral-Small-3.2\"\n548\t      ]\n549\t    },\n550\t    \"tables\": [\n551\t      {\n552\t        \"name\": \"Table S5: Real vs Synthetic Contamination Distribution Comparison\",\n553\t        \"columns\": [\n554\t          \"Distribution\",\n555\t          \"Mean\",\n556\t          \"Std\",\n557\t          \"Median\",\n558\t          \"Q25\",\n559\t          \"Q75\",\n560\t          \"KS_p_vs_real\"\n561\t        ],\n562\t        \"rows\": [\n563\t          [\n564\t            \"Real data\",\n565\t            1.18,\n566\t            0.64,\n567\t            1.05,\n568\t            0.62,\n569\t            1.58,\n570\t            \"—\"\n571\t          ],\n572\t          [\n573\t            \"mvp_001 DGP\",\n574\t            0.5,\n575\t            0.3,\n576\t            0.45,\n577\t            0.28,\n578\t            0.68,\n579\t            0.001\n580\t          ],\n581\t          [\n582\t            \"mvp_002 DGP\",\n583\t            1.5,\n584\t            0.5,\n585\t            1.48,\n586\t            1.15,\n587\t            1.82,\n588\t            0.12\n589\t          ],\n590\t          [\n591\t            \"mvp_003 DGP\",\n592\t            1.2,\n593\t            0.5,\n594\t            1.18,\n595\t            0.82,\n596\t            1.55,\n597\t            0.41\n598\t          ]\n599\t        ]\n600\t      }\n601\t    ],\n602\t    \"figures\": [],\n603\t    \"analysis\": \"真实污染量级与 mvp_003 高度一致（KS p=0.41），远非 mvp_001 的弱污染场景。 这意味着 mvp_003 的合成结果（RMSE −43.8%, τ +6.3pp）是对真实场景的合理预测， real data 上观测到的效应量（RMSE −34.2%, τ +0.06）与之一致但略小， 可归因于真实数据中 confounding 结构不如 DGP 极端。 c_n 与 Elo 正相关（r=0.58）提供了额外的 construct validity： 被更多使用的强模型更可能接触 benchmark data。\\n\\n\\nbest 档假设 c̄≥1.0。c_n_mean=1.18 最接近 mvp_003（c̄=1.2）， KS test p=0.41 表明真实分布与 mvp_003 DGP 不可区分。这是 best 档的核心验证： 真实污染量级确实接近 mvp_003 设定而非 mvp_001（弱），论文 story 完全成立。 高 Elo 模型（GPT-5.5, Claude Opus 4.7, DeepSeek-V4-Pro）c_n 最高（1.4-2.4）， 因为它们训练数据最多、最可能包含 benchmark items。小模型（Phi-4-mini, Llama-3.3-8B） c_n 低（0.1-0.4），因为训练数据量和质量有限，benchmark 泄漏概率低。 这种结构性模式增强了 c_n 估计的 face validity。\\n\"\n604\t  },\n605\t  {\n606\t    \"name\": \"judge_count_sensitivity\",\n607\t    \"description\": \"从 8 judges 中抽取子集（2, 4, 6 judges），对每个子集重新拟合 G-MFRM， 测量 Kendall-τ 随 judge 数量的变化。每个 judge 数量随机抽取 20 次取均值。 确定 G-MFRM 优于 sequential 的最小 judge 数量。\\n\",\n608\t    \"results\": {\n609\t      \"tau_2_judges_gmfrm\": 0.86,\n610\t      \"tau_2_judges_sequential\": 0.84,\n611\t      \"tau_4_judges_gmfrm\": 0.89,\n612\t      \"tau_4_judges_sequential\": 0.85,\n613\t      \"tau_6_judges_gmfrm\": 0.9,\n614\t      \"tau_6_judges_sequential\": 0.85,\n615\t      \"tau_8_judges_gmfrm\": 0.91,\n616\t      \"tau_8_judges_sequential\": 0.85,\n617\t      \"min_judges_for_significant_improvement\": 4,\n618\t      \"delta_tau_2_judges\": 0.02,\n619\t      \"delta_tau_4_judges\": 0.04,\n620\t      \"delta_tau_6_judges\": 0.05,\n621\t      \"delta_tau_8_judges\": 0.06,\n622\t      \"p_value_at_4_judges\": 0.008,\n623\t      \"p_value_at_2_judges\": 0.14,\n624\t      \"convergence_2_judges_max_rhat\": 1.04,\n625\t      \"convergence_4_judges_max_rhat\": 1.03\n626\t    },\n627\t    \"tables\": [\n628\t      {\n629\t        \"name\": \"Table 3: Judge Count Sensitivity Analysis\",\n630\t        \"columns\": [\n631\t          \"N_judges\",\n632\t          \"G-MFRM_τ\",\n633\t          \"Sequential_τ\",\n634\t          \"Δτ\",\n635\t          \"p_value\",\n636\t          \"Max_Rhat\",\n637\t          \"Min_ESS\"\n638\t        ],\n639\t        \"rows\": [\n640\t          [\n641\t            2,\n642\t            \"0.86±0.03\",\n643\t            \"0.84±0.02\",\n644\t            0.02,\n645\t            0.14,\n646\t            1.04,\n647\t            185\n648\t          ],\n649\t          [\n650\t            4,\n651\t            \"0.89±0.02\",\n652\t            \"0.85±0.02\",\n653\t            0.04,\n654\t            0.008,\n655\t            1.03,\n656\t            265\n657\t          ],\n658\t          [\n659\t            6,\n660\t            \"0.90±0.01\",\n661\t            \"0.85±0.01\",\n662\t            0.05,\n663\t            0.001,\n664\t            1.02,\n665\t            298\n666\t          ],\n667\t          [\n668\t            8,\n669\t            \"0.91±0.01\",\n670\t            \"0.85±0.01\",\n671\t            0.06,\n672\t            3.2e-05,\n673\t            1.02,\n674\t            312\n675\t          ]\n676\t        ]\n677\t      }\n678\t    ],\n679\t    \"figures\": [],\n680\t    \"analysis\": \"实用建议：4 judges 是 G-MFRM 优势显著的最低门槛。 这对 practitioner 有价值：即使只有 4 个 judges，joint estimation 也值得。 Sequential 的平坦曲线是 confounding claim 的另一个实证支撑—— 增加数据量（更多 judges）不能修复结构性模型误设。\\n\\n\\nG-MFRM 的优势随 judge 数量增加而单调增长，因为更多 judges 提供了更好的 d_j 和 c_n 可辨识性——judge severity 的 cross-information 帮助分离 confounding。 2 judges 时 G-MFRM 仍优于 sequential（Δτ=0.02），但不显著（p=0.14）， 因为 2 judges 的 d_j 估计不稳定，gating mechanism 无法充分发挥。 4 judges 是临界点（p=0.008<0.01），此后优势稳定。 Sequential 的 τ 对 judge 数量不敏感（0.84-0.85），因为它的 confounding bias 不因更多 judges 而消除——这是结构性问题而非数据量问题。 这一对比直接展示了 joint vs sequential 的本质差异。\\n\"\n681\t  },\n682\t  {\n683\t    \"name\": \"exposure_indicator_ablation\",\n684\t    \"description\": \"Leave-one-out ablation：依次移除 ConStat delta、temporal signal、LogProber Safe Score 中的一个 exposure indicator，重新拟合 G-MFRM，比较 Kendall-τ 变化。 同时测试 single-indicator 版本。\\n\",\n685\t    \"results\": {\n686\t      \"full_composite_tau\": 0.91,\n687\t      \"without_constat_tau\": 0.88,\n688\t      \"without_temporal_tau\": 0.9,\n689\t      \"without_logprober_tau\": 0.9,\n690\t      \"constat_only_tau\": 0.9,\n691\t      \"temporal_only_tau\": 0.87,\n692\t      \"logprober_only_tau\": 0.87,\n693\t      \"constat_marginal_contribution\": 0.03,\n694\t      \"temporal_marginal_contribution\": 0.01,\n695\t      \"logprober_marginal_contribution\": 0.01,\n696\t      \"constat_rank_corr_with_c_n\": 0.81,\n697\t      \"temporal_rank_corr_with_c_n\": 0.62,\n698\t      \"logprober_rank_corr_with_c_n\": 0.59\n699\t    },\n700\t    \"tables\": [\n701\t      {\n702\t        \"name\": \"Table 4: Exposure Indicator Ablation\",\n703\t        \"columns\": [\n704\t          \"Configuration\",\n705\t          \"Indicators_used\",\n706\t          \"Kendall_τ\",\n707\t          \"Δτ_vs_full\",\n708\t          \"Rank_corr_with_c_n\"\n709\t        ],\n710\t        \"rows\": [\n711\t          [\n712\t            \"Full composite\",\n713\t            \"ConStat + Temporal + LogProber\",\n714\t            0.91,\n715\t            \"—\",\n716\t            0.85\n717\t          ],\n718\t          [\n719\t            \"w/o ConStat\",\n720\t            \"Temporal + LogProber\",\n721\t            0.88,\n722\t            -0.03,\n723\t            0.68\n724\t          ],\n725\t          [\n726\t            \"w/o Temporal\",\n727\t            \"ConStat + LogProber\",\n728\t            0.9,\n729\t            -0.01,\n730\t            0.82\n731\t          ],\n732\t          [\n733\t            \"w/o LogProber\",\n734\t            \"ConStat + Temporal\",\n735\t            0.9,\n736\t            -0.01,\n737\t            0.83\n738\t          ],\n739\t          [\n740\t            \"ConStat only\",\n741\t            \"ConStat\",\n742\t            0.9,\n743\t            -0.01,\n744\t            0.81\n745\t          ],\n746\t          [\n747\t            \"Temporal only\",\n748\t            \"Temporal\",\n749\t            0.87,\n750\t            -0.04,\n751\t            0.62\n752\t          ],\n753\t          [\n754\t            \"LogProber only\",\n755\t            \"LogProber\",\n756\t            0.87,\n757\t            -0.04,\n758\t            0.59\n759\t          ],\n760\t          [\n761\t            \"No exposure (MFRM-only)\",\n762\t            \"None\",\n763\t            0.84,\n764\t            -0.07,\n765\t            \"—\"\n766\t          ]\n767\t        ]\n768\t      }\n769\t    ],\n770\t    \"figures\": [],\n771\t    \"analysis\": \"ConStat 是 Stage 2 的支柱，但 G-MFRM 即使在 ConStat 缺失时仍优于 sequential（0.88 > 0.85）， 表明 joint framework 的结构性优势独立于 exposure estimation 质量。 这回应了潜在 reviewer 质疑：\\\"如果 ConStat 不准怎么办？\\\"—— 答案是 G-MFRM 优雅退化但不崩溃。\\n\\n\\nConStat 是最关键的 exposure indicator（marginal contribution +0.03）， 因为它直接测量 behavioral contamination signal（原始 vs rephrased 表现差异）， 与 c_n 的 rank correlation 最高（0.81）。移除 ConStat 后 τ 从 0.91 降至 0.88， 仍优于所有 baselines（best baseline UDA τ=0.86），说明 G-MFRM 的优势 不完全依赖于 exposure estimation 质量——joint calibration 框架本身就有结构性优势。 Temporal 和 LogProber 各贡献 0.01，它们提供的信息与 ConStat 部分重叠。 ConStat-only 版本（τ=0.90）已接近 full composite（0.91）， 进一步确认 ConStat 是 Stage 2 的核心。\\n\"\n772\t  },\n773\t  {\n774\t    \"name\": \"facet_fit_diagnostics\",\n775\t    \"description\": \"报告全部 facets（θ, b, d, c）的 infit/outfit MNSQ， 标记 misfitting elements（MNSQ > 1.3 或 < 0.7）。 比较 Stage 1 person-fit 指标（lz, EMRi）与 Stage 3 c_n 估计的一致性。\\n\",\n776\t    \"results\": {\n777\t      \"theta_infit_mean\": 1.01,\n778\t      \"theta_infit_range\": [\n779\t        0.78,\n780\t        1.25\n781\t      ],\n782\t      \"theta_outfit_mean\": 1.03,\n783\t      \"theta_pct_misfit\": 4.5,\n784\t      \"b_infit_mean\": 1.0,\n785\t      \"b_infit_range\": [\n786\t        0.65,\n787\t        1.42\n788\t      ],\n789\t      \"b_pct_misfit\": 5.2,\n790\t      \"d_infit_mean\": 0.98,\n791\t      \"d_infit_range\": [\n792\t        0.82,\n793\t        1.18\n794\t      ],\n795\t      \"d_pct_misfit\": 0.0,\n796\t      \"c_infit_mean\": 1.02,\n797\t      \"c_pct_misfit\": 9.1,\n798\t      \"lz_c_n_rank_corr\": 0.72,\n799\t      \"emri_c_n_rank_corr\": 0.68,\n800\t      \"pct_agreement_flagged\": 78.3\n801\t    },\n802\t    \"tables\": [\n803\t      {\n804\t        \"name\": \"Table S6: Facet Fit Statistics\",\n805\t        \"columns\": [\n806\t          \"Facet\",\n807\t          \"N\",\n808\t          \"Infit_MNSQ_mean\",\n809\t          \"Infit_MNSQ_range\",\n810\t          \"Outfit_MNSQ_mean\",\n811\t          \"Pct_misfit\"\n812\t        ],\n813\t        \"rows\": [\n814\t          [\n815\t            \"θ (ability)\",\n816\t            22,\n817\t            1.01,\n818\t            \"0.78–1.25\",\n819\t            1.03,\n820\t            4.5\n821\t          ],\n822\t          [\n823\t            \"b (difficulty)\",\n824\t            580,\n825\t            1.0,\n826\t            \"0.65–1.42\",\n827\t            1.02,\n828\t            5.2\n829\t          ],\n830\t          [\n831\t            \"d (severity)\",\n832\t            8,\n833\t            0.98,\n834\t            \"0.82–1.18\",\n835\t            0.99,\n836\t            0.0\n837\t          ],\n838\t          [\n839\t            \"c (contamination)\",\n840\t            22,\n841\t            1.02,\n842\t            \"0.74–1.38\",\n843\t            1.05,\n844\t            9.1\n845\t          ]\n846\t        ]\n847\t      },\n848\t      {\n849\t        \"name\": \"Table S7: Person-Fit vs c_n Convergent Validity\",\n850\t        \"columns\": [\n851\t          \"Metric\",\n852\t          \"Rank_corr_with_c_n\",\n853\t          \"p_value\",\n854\t          \"Pct_overlap_flagged\"\n855\t        ],\n856\t        \"rows\": [\n857\t          [\n858\t            \"lz (person-fit)\",\n859\t            0.72,\n860\t            0.0002,\n861\t            78.3\n862\t          ],\n863\t          [\n864\t            \"EMRi (extended)\",\n865\t            0.68,\n866\t            0.0008,\n867\t            73.9\n868\t          ]\n869\t        ]\n870\t      }\n871\t    ],\n872\t    \"figures\": [],\n873\t    \"analysis\": \"整体拟合质量支撑 framework claim：G-MFRM 不是 overfitting 噪声， 而是合理捕捉了数据结构。c_n 的 9.1% misfit 率可在 Limitations 中坦诚报告， 并指向 rank-k extension 的 future work。person-fit/c_n 的 convergent validity (r=0.72) 是 DG-IRT 迁移成功的额外证据。\\n\\n\\nbest 档下 MFRM 拟合良好：θ 和 d 的 infit/outfit 接近 1.0，misfit 率低。 b (items) 的 misfit 略高（5.2%），因为部分 Arena-Hard items 的难度在 不同 judges 间变异大（某些 items 对某些 judges \\\"特别难评\\\"）。 c_n 的 misfit 率最高（9.1%=2/22 models），因为 rank-1 c_n·e_i 假设 对极端模型（极高或极低污染）拟合不完美——这正是论文中坦诚讨论 rank-1 局限性的位置。 lz 和 c_n 的 rank correlation 0.72 表明传统 person-fit 指标确实能部分捕捉 contamination（因为 contaminated models 在高曝光 items 上表现异常好）， 但 c_n 提供了更结构化的解释。两者 78.3% 的重叠验证了 construct coherence。\\n\"\n874\t  },\n875\t  {\n876\t    \"name\": \"confounding_formal_proposition\",\n877\t    \"description\": \"推导 sequential estimator 在 d_j/c_n·e_i 非正交条件下的一阶 bias 近似。 形式化为 Proposition 1（Section 2）。Monte Carlo 验证 bias 近似精度。\\n\",\n878\t    \"results\": {\n879\t      \"proposition_statement\": \"Under non-orthogonality (Cov(d_j, c_n·e_i) ≠ 0), the bias-first sequential estimator θ̂_seq has first-order bias E[θ̂_seq - θ] ≈ γ·Cov(d_j, c_n·e_i)/Var(d_j) where γ is the contamination gating coefficient. Direction: positive covariance → overestimation of high-contamination models.\\n\",\n880\t      \"mc_n_simulations\": 5000,\n881\t      \"mc_parameter_grid_size\": 50,\n882\t      \"bias_approximation_r2\": 0.94,\n883\t      \"bias_direction_correct_pct\": 97.8,\n884\t      \"max_bias_at_rho_0_6\": 0.31,\n885\t      \"bias_at_rho_0_3\": 0.14,\n886\t      \"real_data_rho\": 0.37,\n887\t      \"real_data_predicted_bias\": 0.17,\n888\t      \"real_data_observed_bias\": 0.19,\n889\t      \"prediction_error_pct\": 10.5\n890\t    },\n891\t    \"tables\": [\n892\t      {\n893\t        \"name\": \"Table S8: Monte Carlo Validation of Bias Approximation\",\n894\t        \"columns\": [\n895\t          \"rho_range\",\n896\t          \"N_sims\",\n897\t          \"Mean_true_bias\",\n898\t          \"Mean_approx_bias\",\n899\t          \"Approx_R2\",\n900\t          \"Direction_accuracy_pct\"\n901\t        ],\n902\t        \"rows\": [\n903\t          [\n904\t            \"[-0.8, -0.4]\",\n905\t            1000,\n906\t            -0.28,\n907\t            -0.26,\n908\t            0.93,\n909\t            98.2\n910\t          ],\n911\t          [\n912\t            \"[-0.4, 0.0]\",\n913\t            1000,\n914\t            -0.09,\n915\t            -0.08,\n916\t            0.95,\n917\t            97.5\n918\t          ],\n919\t          [\n920\t            \"[0.0, 0.4]\",\n921\t            1000,\n922\t            0.1,\n923\t            0.09,\n924\t            0.94,\n925\t            97.8\n926\t          ],\n927\t          [\n928\t            \"[0.4, 0.8]\",\n929\t            1000,\n930\t            0.32,\n931\t            0.3,\n932\t            0.93,\n933\t            97.6\n934\t          ],\n935\t          [\n936\t            \"Overall\",\n937\t            5000,\n938\t            \"—\",\n939\t            \"—\",\n940\t            0.94,\n941\t            97.8\n942\t          ]\n943\t        ]\n944\t      }\n945\t    ],\n946\t    \"figures\": [],\n947\t    \"analysis\": \"Proposition 1 将 confounding claim 从实证观察提升为理论结果， MC 验证确认近似在实际参数范围内高精度（R²=0.94）。 real data 上 predicted vs observed bias 的一致性（10.5% error） 提供了 \\\"theory predicts, data confirms\\\" 的强叙事弧线。 Section 2 可以先展示 proposition，再用 exp-003 的 bias scatter 作为实证验证。\\n\\n\\n一阶 bias 近似基于 omitted variable bias 的经典结果（Angrist & Pischke 框架 在 psychometric context 的适配）。R²=0.94 表明一阶近似在实际参数范围内精度高。 关键洞察：bias 方向由 Cov(d_j, c_n·e_i) 决定——当严格 judges（高 d_j） 与高污染模型×高曝光 items 的交互为正时，sequential 高估高污染模型。 真实数据 ρ=0.37 > 0 预测正向 bias 0.17 std units，观测值 0.19 std units， 预测误差仅 10.5%——形式化命题在真实数据上得到量化验证。 这为 Section 2 提供了理论 + 实证双重论证。\\n\"\n948\t  },\n949\t  {\n950\t    \"name\": \"wildbench_replication\",\n951\t    \"description\": \"在 WildBench 上复制 G-MFRM pipeline：收集 8 judges × 22 models 评分， ConStat exposure estimation，三阶段拟合，baseline 比较。 验证跨 benchmark 泛化性。\\n\",\n952\t    \"results\": {\n953\t      \"wildbench_n_items\": 1024,\n954\t      \"kendall_tau_gmfrm_wildbench\": 0.89,\n955\t      \"kendall_tau_sequential_wildbench\": 0.84,\n956\t      \"kendall_tau_uda_wildbench\": 0.85,\n957\t      \"delta_tau_vs_best_baseline_wildbench\": 0.04,\n958\t      \"wilcoxon_p_gmfrm_vs_seq_wildbench\": 0.00021,\n959\t      \"c_n_mean_wildbench\": 0.95,\n960\t      \"c_n_rank_corr_cross_benchmark\": 0.82,\n961\t      \"convergence_max_rhat_wildbench\": 1.02,\n962\t      \"convergence_min_ess_wildbench\": 278\n963\t    },\n964\t    \"tables\": [\n965\t      {\n966\t        \"name\": \"Table 5: Cross-Benchmark Replication (WildBench)\",\n967\t        \"columns\": [\n968\t          \"Method\",\n969\t          \"WildBench_τ\",\n970\t          \"MT-Bench_τ\",\n971\t          \"Arena-Hard_τ\"\n972\t        ],\n973\t        \"rows\": [\n974\t          [\n975\t            \"Raw Average\",\n976\t            0.8,\n977\t            0.8,\n978\t            0.83\n979\t          ],\n980\t          [\n981\t            \"Sequential\",\n982\t            0.84,\n983\t            0.84,\n984\t            0.86\n985\t          ],\n986\t          [\n987\t            \"UDA\",\n988\t            0.85,\n989\t            0.85,\n990\t            0.87\n991\t          ],\n992\t          [\n993\t            \"**G-MFRM**\",\n994\t            \"**0.89**\",\n995\t            \"**0.90**\",\n996\t            \"**0.91**\"\n997\t          ]\n998\t        ]\n999\t      }\n1000\t    ],\n1001\t    \"figures\": [],\n1002\t    \"analysis\": \"跨 benchmark 泛化成功：G-MFRM 在第三个独立 benchmark 上同样显著优于全部 baselines。 c_n 跨 benchmark 一致性（r=0.82）是论文的加分项—— 说明 contamination susceptibility 是模型的稳定属性，G-MFRM 估计的不是 benchmark-specific 噪声。\\n\\n\\nWildBench τ=0.89 略低于 MT-Bench+Arena-Hard 的 0.91， 因为 WildBench items 更 open-ended、scoring 更主观， 引入了 G-MFRM 无法完全捕捉的 noise。但仍显著优于全部 baselines（Δτ=0.04）。 c_n_mean=0.95 略低于主数据集的 1.18，因为 WildBench 较新（2024）， 部分 items 未被充分泄漏。跨 benchmark c_n rank correlation 0.82 表明 contamination 是模型属性（不是 benchmark 属性）， 支撑 c_n 作为 meaningful latent trait 的解读。\\n\"\n1003\t  },\n1004\t  {\n1005\t    \"name\": \"adversarial_robustness\",\n1006\t    \"description\": \"模拟 Wang et al. (ICLR 2026) 的 adversarial contamination 场景： 对 target model 注入 benchmark items（0%, 5%, 10%, 20% training data）， 测试 G-MFRM c_n 估计是否正确反映注入量， 以及 θ 估计是否对 adversarial contamination 鲁棒。\\n\",\n1007\t    \"results\": {\n1008\t      \"c_n_at_0pct_injection\": 0.15,\n1009\t      \"c_n_at_5pct_injection\": 0.82,\n1010\t      \"c_n_at_10pct_injection\": 1.45,\n1011\t      \"c_n_at_20pct_injection\": 2.18,\n1012\t      \"c_n_injection_correlation\": 0.97,\n1013\t      \"theta_bias_at_0pct\": 0.02,\n1014\t      \"theta_bias_at_5pct\": 0.05,\n1015\t      \"theta_bias_at_10pct\": 0.08,\n1016\t      \"theta_bias_at_20pct\": 0.14,\n1017\t      \"theta_bias_sequential_at_20pct\": 0.52,\n1018\t      \"robustness_ratio_20pct\": 3.71,\n1019\t      \"auc_detecting_contaminated\": 0.94\n1020\t    },\n1021\t    \"tables\": [\n1022\t      {\n1023\t        \"name\": \"Table S9: Adversarial Robustness — θ Bias Under Controlled Contamination\",\n1024\t        \"columns\": [\n1025\t          \"Injection_pct\",\n1026\t          \"G-MFRM_c_n\",\n1027\t          \"G-MFRM_θ_bias\",\n1028\t          \"Sequential_θ_bias\",\n1029\t          \"Robustness_ratio\"\n1030\t        ],\n1031\t        \"rows\": [\n1032\t          [\n1033\t            0,\n1034\t            0.15,\n1035\t            0.02,\n1036\t            0.03,\n1037\t            1.5\n1038\t          ],\n1039\t          [\n1040\t            5,\n1041\t            0.82,\n1042\t            0.05,\n1043\t            0.18,\n1044\t            3.6\n1045\t          ],\n1046\t          [\n1047\t            10,\n1048\t            1.45,\n1049\t            0.08,\n1050\t            0.34,\n1051\t            4.25\n1052\t          ],\n1053\t          [\n1054\t            20,\n1055\t            2.18,\n1056\t            0.14,\n1057\t            0.52,\n1058\t            3.71\n1059\t          ]\n1060\t        ]\n1061\t      }\n1062\t    ],\n1063\t    \"figures\": [],\n1064\t    \"analysis\": \"Adversarial robustness 是 reviewer concern 的预防性回应。 G-MFRM 在极端场景（20% injection）下 θ bias 仅为 sequential 的 1/4， 且 c_n 可作为 post-hoc contamination audit 工具（AUC=0.94）。 这将 G-MFRM 从 \\\"evaluation correction method\\\" 提升为 \\\"contamination-aware evaluation framework\\\"。\\n\\nG-MFRM 的 gating mechanism 设计上就是为了 absorb contamination effect into c_n， 所以 c_n 与 injection rate 高度相关（r=0.97）是预期中的。 θ bias 在 20% injection 时仅 0.14（vs sequential 的 0.52）， 因为 G-MFRM 将 contamination inflation 归因于 c_n 而非 θ。 robustness ratio 3.71× 意味着 G-MFRM 的 θ 偏差仅为 sequential 的 27%。 AUC=0.94 表明 c_n 可以作为 contamination detection 工具， 这为论文的 practical impact 增加了一个维度。 注意：这是在 controlled setting（已知注入量）的 validation， 与真实场景的 unknown contamination 有区别，需在论文中说明。\\n\"\n1065\t  }\n1066\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c07c60bb-447f-4ecc-97a6-9e6b367c22a6","uuid":"5d37e2c5-0329-4b61-8fa9-569365376ce7","timestamp":"2026-05-21T21:02:36.071Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-prod43/projects/gated_mfrm_judge_bias/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260521T204917/best/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"multi_judge_data_collection\",\n    \"description\": \"8 judges（GPT-5.5, Claude Opus 4.7, Claude Sonnet 4.6, DeepSeek-V4-Pro, Qwen3-235B-A22B, Qwen3.6-27B, Llama 4 Maverick, Gemini 2.5 Pro） 评估 22 个 target models，MT-Bench 80 items + Arena-Hard 500 items， position swap 产生双向评分。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_judges\": 8,\n      \"n_target_models\": 22,\n      \"n_items_mtbench\": 80,\n      \"n_items_arenahard\": 500,\n      \"total_judgments_mtbench\": 28160,\n      \"total_judgments_arenahard\": 176000,\n      \"missing_rate_pct\": 1.8,\n      \"position_bias_avg_swap_disagreement_pct\": 12.5,\n      \"api_cost_usd\": 780,\n      \"vllm_gpu_hours\": 105,\n      \"inter_judge_agreement_fleiss_kappa\": 0.41,\n      \"judge_severity_range_raw_std\": 0.82\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table S1: Data Collection Summary\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Judge\",\n          \"Provider\",\n          \"Type\",\n          \"MT-Bench_judgments\",\n          \"Arena-Hard_judgments\",\n          \"Missing_pct\",\n          \"Avg_score\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"GPT-5.5\",\n            \"OpenAI\",\n            \"API\",\n            3520,\n            22000,\n            1.2,\n            7.84\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Claude Opus 4.7\",\n            \"Anthropic\",\n            \"API\",\n            3520,\n            22000,\n            0.8,\n            7.52\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Claude Sonnet 4.6\",\n            \"Anthropic\",\n            \"API\",\n            3520,\n            22000,\n            1.1,\n            7.71\n          ],\n          [\n            \"DeepSeek-V4-Pro\",\n            \"DeepSeek\",\n            \"API\",\n            3520,\n            22000,\n            2.0,\n            7.63\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Qwen3-235B-A22B\",\n            \"Alibaba\",\n            \"vLLM\",\n            3520,\n            22000,\n            2.5,\n            7.45\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Qwen3.6-27B\",\n            \"Alibaba\",\n            \"vLLM\",\n            3520,\n            22000,\n            3.1,\n            7.28\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Llama 4 Maverick\",\n            \"Meta\",\n            \"vLLM\",\n            3520,\n            22000,\n            2.8,\n            7.39\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Gemini 2.5 Pro\",\n            \"Google\",\n            \"API\",\n            3520,\n            22000,\n            1.5,\n            7.68\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"数据质量充分支撑后续全部实验。缺失率 1.8% 可用 MCMC 内自然处理（missing at random 假设合理， 缺失主要来自 API timeout 而非 systematic）。8 judges 的 severity 分布有足够变异（std=0.82）， 开源 judges（Qwen3.6-27B, Llama 4 Maverick）系统性偏低 0.3-0.4 分， 为 d_j 估计提供了清晰信号。\\n\\n\\nbest 档假设数据收集无重大缺失。8 个 judges 涵盖 4 家厂商 + 3 个开源， 缺失率 <2% 因 API 和 vLLM 基础设施成熟。position swap disagreement ~12.5% 符合已知 LLM positional bias 文献（Zheng et al. 2023 报告 10-15%）。 inter-judge Fleiss κ≈0.41 处于 \\\"moderate agreement\\\" 范围，这正是 G-MFRM 需要的场景——若 judges 高度一致则无需建模 severity。 judge severity raw std=0.82 表明 judges 间存在可量化的系统性差异， 为后续 MFRM 的 d_j 估计提供充分变异。API 成本低于 $900 预算。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"constat_exposure_estimation\",\n    \"description\": \"对 MT-Bench 80 + Arena-Hard 500 items 生成 reference variants（GPT-5.5 rephrased）， 人工抽检 50 items 验证语义等价，运行 ConStat pipeline 计算 per-item exposure e_i， 结合 temporal signals（release date proximity）形成 composite exposure indicator。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_items_total\": 580,\n      \"n_reference_variants_per_item\": 3,\n      \"human_equivalence_check_n\": 50,\n      \"human_equivalence_pass_rate_pct\": 94.0,\n      \"constat_delta_mean\": 0.38,\n      \"constat_delta_std\": 0.27,\n      \"constat_rank_corr_with_temporal\": 0.72,\n      \"composite_e_i_mean\": 0.55,\n      \"composite_e_i_std\": 0.31,\n      \"items_high_exposure_pct\": 28.4,\n      \"items_low_exposure_pct\": 35.2,\n      \"mtbench_avg_e_i\": 0.68,\n      \"arenahard_avg_e_i\": 0.49\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table S2: Exposure Estimation Summary by Benchmark\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Benchmark\",\n          \"N_items\",\n          \"Mean_e_i\",\n          \"Std_e_i\",\n          \"High_exposure_pct\",\n          \"ConStat_delta_mean\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"MT-Bench\",\n            80,\n            0.68,\n            0.24,\n            42.5,\n            0.51\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Arena-Hard\",\n            500,\n            0.49,\n            0.31,\n            25.2,\n            0.34\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Combined\",\n            580,\n            0.52,\n            0.3,\n            28.4,\n            0.36\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Exposure estimation 质量足够支撑 Stage 2 anchoring。MT-Bench 的高曝光占比（42.5%） 和 Arena-Hard 的相对低曝光形成了自然对比，有利于 contamination 效应的识别。 Composite indicator 结合了 ConStat 的 behavioral signal 和 temporal 的 prior information， 比单独使用任一信号更鲁棒。这为 exp-003 的 Stage 2 提供了可靠的 external anchor。\\n\\n\\nbest 档假设 ConStat e_i 估计与真实曝光高度一致（rank correlation ≥ 0.85）。 MT-Bench 作为 2023 年发布的广泛使用 benchmark，items 曝光量显著高于 Arena-Hard（动态更新），体现为 MT-Bench avg e_i=0.68 > Arena-Hard 0.49。 ConStat delta 与 temporal signal 相关 r=0.72 表明两个独立信号的一致性， 增强了 composite indicator 的可信度。human equivalence 94% pass rate 表明 reference variants 质量高，未引入语义偏移。28.4% items 高曝光 提供了充足的 contamination signal 变异范围。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"gmfrm_real_data_fit\",\n    \"description\": \"三阶段 pipeline 在真实数据上拟合：Stage 1 MFRM 估计 θ,b,d； Stage 2 用 exp-002 的 e_i 作为 external anchor； Stage 3 joint gated model 同时估计所有 facets 含 latent c_n。 NumPyro MCMC (warmup=2000, samples=4000, chains=4, NCP, target_accept=0.95)。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"convergence_max_rhat\": 1.02,\n      \"convergence_min_ess\": 312,\n      \"convergence_all_params_rhat_below_1_05\": true,\n      \"convergence_pct_params_rhat_below_1_01\": 87.3,\n      \"real_c_n_mean\": 1.18,\n      \"real_c_n_std\": 0.64,\n      \"real_c_n_median\": 1.05,\n      \"pct_models_c_n_above_0_8\": 45.5,\n      \"pct_models_c_n_above_1_5\": 18.2,\n      \"c_n_range\": [\n        0.12,\n        2.41\n      ],\n      \"kendall_tau_arena_mtbench\": 0.91,\n      \"kendall_tau_arena_arenahard\": 0.9,\n      \"kendall_tau_arena_combined\": 0.91,\n      \"spearman_rho_arena_combined\": 0.96,\n      \"kendall_tau_sequential_combined\": 0.85,\n      \"delta_tau_vs_sequential\": 0.06,\n      \"rmse_theta_vs_sequential_reduction_pct\": 34.2,\n      \"wilcoxon_p_joint_vs_seq\": 3.2e-05,\n      \"scatter_pearson_r_seq_bias\": 0.61,\n      \"confounding_theta_rmse_degradation_pct\": 28.5,\n      \"d_j_c_n_e_i_correlation_abs\": 0.37,\n      \"runtime_hours\": 2.8,\n      \"total_mcmc_samples\": 16000\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 1 (Main): Model Ability Estimates — G-MFRM vs Sequential\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Model\",\n          \"Arena_Elo\",\n          \"G-MFRM_θ\",\n          \"Sequential_θ\",\n          \"Raw_Avg\",\n          \"c_n_estimate\"\n        ],\n        \"note\": \"22 rows, top-5 and bottom-5 shown for illustration\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"GPT-5.5\",\n            1320,\n            1.82,\n            1.95,\n            8.12,\n            1.63\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Claude Opus 4.7\",\n            1305,\n            1.74,\n            1.82,\n            7.98,\n            1.41\n          ],\n          [\n            \"DeepSeek-V4-Pro\",\n            1285,\n            1.61,\n            1.73,\n            7.85,\n            1.52\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Gemini 2.5 Pro\",\n            1275,\n            1.55,\n            1.58,\n            7.79,\n            0.89\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Claude Sonnet 4.6\",\n            1260,\n            1.48,\n            1.51,\n            7.72,\n            1.15\n          ],\n          [\n            \"...\",\n            \"...\",\n            \"...\",\n            \"...\",\n            \"...\",\n            \"...\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Phi-4-mini\",\n            1085,\n            0.52,\n            0.48,\n            6.41,\n            0.35\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Llama-3.3-8B\",\n            1065,\n            0.38,\n            0.41,\n            6.22,\n            0.28\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table S3: MCMC Convergence Diagnostics Summary\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Parameter_group\",\n          \"N_params\",\n          \"Max_Rhat\",\n          \"Min_ESS\",\n          \"Median_ESS\",\n          \"Pct_Rhat_below_1_01\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"theta (ability)\",\n            22,\n            1.01,\n            412,\n            1850,\n            95.5\n          ],\n          [\n            \"b (difficulty)\",\n            580,\n            1.02,\n            312,\n            890,\n            85.2\n          ],\n          [\n            \"d (severity)\",\n            8,\n            1.0,\n            2450,\n            3100,\n            100.0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"c (contamination)\",\n            22,\n            1.02,\n            345,\n            1620,\n            86.4\n          ],\n          [\n            \"sigma_priors\",\n            4,\n            1.01,\n            1890,\n            2340,\n            100.0\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"核心发现：真实数据上 c̄=1.18 确认污染非边缘现象，G-MFRM 显著优于 sequential（τ +0.06, p=3.2e-5）。 confounding 在真实数据上通过三条证据链确认：(1) |ρ|=0.37 表明 d_j 与 c_n·e_i 非正交， (2) RMSE degradation 28.5% 表明忽略任一 facet 导致显著偏差， (3) bias scatter r=0.61 表明 sequential 对高污染模型系统性高估。 收敛良好（R̂≤1.02, ESS≥312），支撑 framework claim。\\n\\n\\nbest 档核心假设：真实 c̄≥1.0。c_n_mean=1.18 落在 [1.0, 2.0] 范围内， 接近 mvp_003 设定（mvp_003 DGP 中 c_n~N(1.2,0.5)），表明真实污染量级 确实不是边缘现象。45.5% 模型 c_n>0.8（远超 30% 阈值），说明污染在主流模型中普遍存在。 收敛优于 mvp_003（R̂=1.02 < 1.03），因为真实数据的 N=580 items 远多于 合成数据的 100 items，提供了更多信息量。ESS=312 > 200 阈值， real data 的 item 数量和 judge 数量给 MCMC 更充分的似然信号。 Kendall-τ=0.91 vs sequential 0.85，delta=0.06 落在 [0.04, 0.10] 范围中部， 因为真实数据噪声高于合成但 contamination 量级充足。 |ρ(d_j, c_n·e_i)|=0.37 > 0.3 阈值——严格 judges 倾向于对高污染模型给出更极端分数， confounding 在真实数据上可观测。RMSE degradation 28.5% < mvp_003 的 43.8% 但仍 >20% 阈值，因为真实数据中 confounding 结构不如合成 DGP 极端但仍显著。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"baseline_comparison\",\n    \"description\": \"在同一数据上比较 G-MFRM 与 7 个 baselines： (1) Raw multi-judge average, (2) MFRM-only, (3) Sequential pipeline, (4) CyclicJudge, (5) DCR Factor, (6) UDA, (7) Preference Leakage calibration。 主指标 Kendall-τ 和 Spearman-ρ with Chatbot Arena votes， 分 MT-Bench 和 Arena-Hard 两个 benchmark 报告。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"raw_average_tau\": 0.82,\n      \"mfrm_only_tau\": 0.84,\n      \"sequential_tau\": 0.85,\n      \"cyclicjudge_tau\": 0.84,\n      \"dcr_factor_tau\": 0.83,\n      \"uda_tau\": 0.86,\n      \"pref_leakage_tau\": 0.83,\n      \"gmfrm_tau\": 0.91,\n      \"raw_average_rho\": 0.89,\n      \"mfrm_only_rho\": 0.91,\n      \"sequential_rho\": 0.92,\n      \"cyclicjudge_rho\": 0.91,\n      \"dcr_factor_rho\": 0.9,\n      \"uda_rho\": 0.93,\n      \"pref_leakage_rho\": 0.9,\n      \"gmfrm_rho\": 0.96,\n      \"best_baseline_name\": \"UDA\",\n      \"best_baseline_tau\": 0.86,\n      \"delta_tau_vs_best_baseline\": 0.05,\n      \"wilcoxon_p_gmfrm_vs_uda\": 0.00087,\n      \"wilcoxon_p_gmfrm_vs_sequential\": 3.2e-05,\n      \"wilcoxon_p_gmfrm_vs_raw\": 1.4e-06,\n      \"delta_tau_95ci\": [\n        0.02,\n        0.08\n      ]\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 2 (Main): Baseline Comparison — Kendall-τ with Chatbot Arena\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Method\",\n          \"Bias_Correction\",\n          \"Contam_Correction\",\n          \"Joint\",\n          \"MT-Bench_τ\",\n          \"Arena-Hard_τ\",\n          \"Combined_τ\",\n          \"Combined_ρ\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Raw Average\",\n            \"✗\",\n            \"✗\",\n            \"✗\",\n            0.8,\n            0.83,\n            0.82,\n            0.89\n          ],\n          [\n            \"MFRM-only\",\n            \"✓\",\n            \"✗\",\n            \"—\",\n            0.83,\n            0.85,\n            0.84,\n            0.91\n          ],\n          [\n            \"CyclicJudge\",\n            \"✓\",\n            \"✗\",\n            \"—\",\n            0.82,\n            0.85,\n            0.84,\n            0.91\n          ],\n          [\n            \"DCR Factor\",\n            \"✗\",\n            \"✓\",\n            \"—\",\n            0.81,\n            0.84,\n            0.83,\n            0.9\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Pref Leakage\",\n            \"✗\",\n            \"✓\",\n            \"—\",\n            0.82,\n            0.84,\n            0.83,\n            0.9\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Sequential\",\n            \"✓\",\n            \"✓\",\n            \"✗\",\n            0.84,\n            0.86,\n            0.85,\n            0.92\n          ],\n          [\n            \"UDA\",\n            \"✓(neural)\",\n            \"✗\",\n            \"—\",\n            0.85,\n            0.87,\n            0.86,\n            0.93\n          ],\n          [\n            \"**G-MFRM (ours)**\",\n            \"✓\",\n            \"✓\",\n            \"✓\",\n            \"**0.90**\",\n            \"**0.91**\",\n            \"**0.91**\",\n            \"**0.96**\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table S4: Pairwise Significance (Wilcoxon p-values, G-MFRM vs each baseline)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Baseline\",\n          \"p_value_tau\",\n          \"p_value_rho\",\n          \"Significant_at_0_01\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Raw Average\",\n            1.4e-06,\n            2.1e-06,\n            \"✓\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"MFRM-only\",\n            5.8e-05,\n            8.3e-05,\n            \"✓\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"CyclicJudge\",\n            7.2e-05,\n            0.00011,\n            \"✓\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"DCR Factor\",\n            2.3e-05,\n            3.5e-05,\n            \"✓\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Pref Leakage\",\n            3.1e-05,\n            4.7e-05,\n            \"✓\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Sequential\",\n            3.2e-05,\n            4.9e-05,\n            \"✓\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"UDA\",\n            0.00087,\n            0.0012,\n            \"✓\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"G-MFRM 在全部 7 baselines 上显著优于，最强 baseline UDA 的差距也在统计上显著（p<0.001）。 关键观察：bias-only 方法（MFRM, CyclicJudge）和 contam-only 方法（DCR, PrefLeakage） 性能相近（τ=0.83-0.84），sequential 小幅提升至 0.85 但受 confounding 限制， 只有 joint estimation 实现了 τ=0.91 的跳跃。这一模式直接支撑 confounding claim： sequential 无法完全解决两个 facet 的交互效应。\\n\\n\\nbest 档下 G-MFRM τ=0.91 落在 [0.88, 0.94] 范围，best baseline τ=0.86 落在 [0.82, 0.87] 范围。 UDA 是最强 baseline（τ=0.86）因为其 neural K-factor 部分捕捉了 judge 间差异， 但它是 black-box 且 contamination-unaware，无法处理 c_n 导致的系统性偏差。 CyclicJudge（τ=0.84）消除了平均 judge bias 但无法捕捉 item-specific severity 差异。 DCR（τ=0.83）仅建模 contamination 而忽略 judge severity，吸收了部分 d_j 效应。 Sequential（τ=0.85）优于单独 correction 但仍受 confounding bias 影响。 MFRM-only（τ=0.84）与 CyclicJudge 相当，因为两者都只建模 judge 效应。 delta=0.05 vs UDA 在 bootstrap 95% CI [0.02, 0.08] 中显著， Wilcoxon p=8.7e-4 落在 [1e-6, 0.001] 范围内。 G-MFRM 在所有 7 baselines 上显著优于，支撑 headline claim。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"contamination_magnitude_calibration\",\n    \"description\": \"将 exp-003 估计的真实 c_n 分布与 mvp_001/002/003 的合成 DGP 设定对比， 确定真实污染量级落在哪个区间，评估对论文 claim 强度的影响。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"real_c_n_mean\": 1.18,\n      \"real_c_n_std\": 0.64,\n      \"real_c_n_median\": 1.05,\n      \"closest_mvp\": \"mvp_003\",\n      \"mvp_001_c_mean\": 0.5,\n      \"mvp_002_c_mean\": 1.5,\n      \"mvp_003_c_mean\": 1.2,\n      \"distance_to_mvp_003\": 0.02,\n      \"distance_to_mvp_001\": 0.68,\n      \"distance_to_mvp_002\": 0.32,\n      \"ks_test_vs_mvp_003_p\": 0.41,\n      \"pct_models_in_mvp_001_regime\": 22.7,\n      \"pct_models_in_mvp_003_regime\": 54.5,\n      \"pct_models_in_mvp_002_regime\": 22.7,\n      \"top3_contaminated_models\": [\n        \"GPT-5.5\",\n        \"DeepSeek-V4-Pro\",\n        \"Claude Opus 4.7\"\n      ],\n      \"top3_clean_models\": [\n        \"Phi-4-mini\",\n        \"Llama-3.3-8B\",\n        \"Mistral-Small-3.2\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table S5: Real vs Synthetic Contamination Distribution Comparison\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Distribution\",\n          \"Mean\",\n          \"Std\",\n          \"Median\",\n          \"Q25\",\n          \"Q75\",\n          \"KS_p_vs_real\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Real data\",\n            1.18,\n            0.64,\n            1.05,\n            0.62,\n            1.58,\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"mvp_001 DGP\",\n            0.5,\n            0.3,\n            0.45,\n            0.28,\n            0.68,\n            0.001\n          ],\n          [\n            \"mvp_002 DGP\",\n            1.5,\n            0.5,\n            1.48,\n            1.15,\n            1.82,\n            0.12\n          ],\n          [\n            \"mvp_003 DGP\",\n            1.2,\n            0.5,\n            1.18,\n            0.82,\n            1.55,\n            0.41\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"真实污染量级与 mvp_003 高度一致（KS p=0.41），远非 mvp_001 的弱污染场景。 这意味着 mvp_003 的合成结果（RMSE −43.8%, τ +6.3pp）是对真实场景的合理预测， real data 上观测到的效应量（RMSE −34.2%, τ +0.06）与之一致但略小， 可归因于真实数据中 confounding 结构不如 DGP 极端。 c_n 与 Elo 正相关（r=0.58）提供了额外的 construct validity： 被更多使用的强模型更可能接触 benchmark data。\\n\\n\\nbest 档假设 c̄≥1.0。c_n_mean=1.18 最接近 mvp_003（c̄=1.2）， KS test p=0.41 表明真实分布与 mvp_003 DGP 不可区分。这是 best 档的核心验证： 真实污染量级确实接近 mvp_003 设定而非 mvp_001（弱），论文 story 完全成立。 高 Elo 模型（GPT-5.5, Claude Opus 4.7, DeepSeek-V4-Pro）c_n 最高（1.4-2.4）， 因为它们训练数据最多、最可能包含 benchmark items。小模型（Phi-4-mini, Llama-3.3-8B） c_n 低（0.1-0.4），因为训练数据量和质量有限，benchmark 泄漏概率低。 这种结构性模式增强了 c_n 估计的 face validity。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"judge_count_sensitivity\",\n    \"description\": \"从 8 judges 中抽取子集（2, 4, 6 judges），对每个子集重新拟合 G-MFRM， 测量 Kendall-τ 随 judge 数量的变化。每个 judge 数量随机抽取 20 次取均值。 确定 G-MFRM 优于 sequential 的最小 judge 数量。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"tau_2_judges_gmfrm\": 0.86,\n      \"tau_2_judges_sequential\": 0.84,\n      \"tau_4_judges_gmfrm\": 0.89,\n      \"tau_4_judges_sequential\": 0.85,\n      \"tau_6_judges_gmfrm\": 0.9,\n      \"tau_6_judges_sequential\": 0.85,\n      \"tau_8_judges_gmfrm\": 0.91,\n      \"tau_8_judges_sequential\": 0.85,\n      \"min_judges_for_significant_improvement\": 4,\n      \"delta_tau_2_judges\": 0.02,\n      \"delta_tau_4_judges\": 0.04,\n      \"delta_tau_6_judges\": 0.05,\n      \"delta_tau_8_judges\": 0.06,\n      \"p_value_at_4_judges\": 0.008,\n      \"p_value_at_2_judges\": 0.14,\n      \"convergence_2_judges_max_rhat\": 1.04,\n      \"convergence_4_judges_max_rhat\": 1.03\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 3: Judge Count Sensitivity Analysis\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"N_judges\",\n          \"G-MFRM_τ\",\n          \"Sequential_τ\",\n          \"Δτ\",\n          \"p_value\",\n          \"Max_Rhat\",\n          \"Min_ESS\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            2,\n            \"0.86±0.03\",\n            \"0.84±0.02\",\n            0.02,\n            0.14,\n            1.04,\n            185\n          ],\n          [\n            4,\n            \"0.89±0.02\",\n            \"0.85±0.02\",\n            0.04,\n            0.008,\n            1.03,\n            265\n          ],\n          [\n            6,\n            \"0.90±0.01\",\n            \"0.85±0.01\",\n            0.05,\n            0.001,\n            1.02,\n            298\n          ],\n          [\n            8,\n            \"0.91±0.01\",\n            \"0.85±0.01\",\n            0.06,\n            3.2e-05,\n            1.02,\n            312\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"实用建议：4 judges 是 G-MFRM 优势显著的最低门槛。 这对 practitioner 有价值：即使只有 4 个 judges，joint estimation 也值得。 Sequential 的平坦曲线是 confounding claim 的另一个实证支撑—— 增加数据量（更多 judges）不能修复结构性模型误设。\\n\\n\\nG-MFRM 的优势随 judge 数量增加而单调增长，因为更多 judges 提供了更好的 d_j 和 c_n 可辨识性——judge severity 的 cross-information 帮助分离 confounding。 2 judges 时 G-MFRM 仍优于 sequential（Δτ=0.02），但不显著（p=0.14）， 因为 2 judges 的 d_j 估计不稳定，gating mechanism 无法充分发挥。 4 judges 是临界点（p=0.008<0.01），此后优势稳定。 Sequential 的 τ 对 judge 数量不敏感（0.84-0.85），因为它的 confounding bias 不因更多 judges 而消除——这是结构性问题而非数据量问题。 这一对比直接展示了 joint vs sequential 的本质差异。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"exposure_indicator_ablation\",\n    \"description\": \"Leave-one-out ablation：依次移除 ConStat delta、temporal signal、LogProber Safe Score 中的一个 exposure indicator，重新拟合 G-MFRM，比较 Kendall-τ 变化。 同时测试 single-indicator 版本。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"full_composite_tau\": 0.91,\n      \"without_constat_tau\": 0.88,\n      \"without_temporal_tau\": 0.9,\n      \"without_logprober_tau\": 0.9,\n      \"constat_only_tau\": 0.9,\n      \"temporal_only_tau\": 0.87,\n      \"logprober_only_tau\": 0.87,\n      \"constat_marginal_contribution\": 0.03,\n      \"temporal_marginal_contribution\": 0.01,\n      \"logprober_marginal_contribution\": 0.01,\n      \"constat_rank_corr_with_c_n\": 0.81,\n      \"temporal_rank_corr_with_c_n\": 0.62,\n      \"logprober_rank_corr_with_c_n\": 0.59\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 4: Exposure Indicator Ablation\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Configuration\",\n          \"Indicators_used\",\n          \"Kendall_τ\",\n          \"Δτ_vs_full\",\n          \"Rank_corr_with_c_n\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Full composite\",\n            \"ConStat + Temporal + LogProber\",\n            0.91,\n            \"—\",\n            0.85\n          ],\n          [\n            \"w/o ConStat\",\n            \"Temporal + LogProber\",\n            0.88,\n            -0.03,\n            0.68\n          ],\n          [\n            \"w/o Temporal\",\n            \"ConStat + LogProber\",\n            0.9,\n            -0.01,\n            0.82\n          ],\n          [\n            \"w/o LogProber\",\n            \"ConStat + Temporal\",\n            0.9,\n            -0.01,\n            0.83\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ConStat only\",\n            \"ConStat\",\n            0.9,\n            -0.01,\n            0.81\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Temporal only\",\n            \"Temporal\",\n            0.87,\n            -0.04,\n            0.62\n          ],\n          [\n            \"LogProber only\",\n            \"LogProber\",\n            0.87,\n            -0.04,\n            0.59\n          ],\n          [\n            \"No exposure (MFRM-only)\",\n            \"None\",\n            0.84,\n            -0.07,\n            \"—\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"ConStat 是 Stage 2 的支柱，但 G-MFRM 即使在 ConStat 缺失时仍优于 sequential（0.88 > 0.85）， 表明 joint framework 的结构性优势独立于 exposure estimation 质量。 这回应了潜在 reviewer 质疑：\\\"如果 ConStat 不准怎么办？\\\"—— 答案是 G-MFRM 优雅退化但不崩溃。\\n\\n\\nConStat 是最关键的 exposure indicator（marginal contribution +0.03）， 因为它直接测量 behavioral contamination signal（原始 vs rephrased 表现差异）， 与 c_n 的 rank correlation 最高（0.81）。移除 ConStat 后 τ 从 0.91 降至 0.88， 仍优于所有 baselines（best baseline UDA τ=0.86），说明 G-MFRM 的优势 不完全依赖于 exposure estimation 质量——joint calibration 框架本身就有结构性优势。 Temporal 和 LogProber 各贡献 0.01，它们提供的信息与 ConStat 部分重叠。 ConStat-only 版本（τ=0.90）已接近 full composite（0.91）， 进一步确认 ConStat 是 Stage 2 的核心。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"facet_fit_diagnostics\",\n    \"description\": \"报告全部 facets（θ, b, d, c）的 infit/outfit MNSQ， 标记 misfitting elements（MNSQ > 1.3 或 < 0.7）。 比较 Stage 1 person-fit 指标（lz, EMRi）与 Stage 3 c_n 估计的一致性。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"theta_infit_mean\": 1.01,\n      \"theta_infit_range\": [\n        0.78,\n        1.25\n      ],\n      \"theta_outfit_mean\": 1.03,\n      \"theta_pct_misfit\": 4.5,\n      \"b_infit_mean\": 1.0,\n      \"b_infit_range\": [\n        0.65,\n        1.42\n      ],\n      \"b_pct_misfit\": 5.2,\n      \"d_infit_mean\": 0.98,\n      \"d_infit_range\": [\n        0.82,\n        1.18\n      ],\n      \"d_pct_misfit\": 0.0,\n      \"c_infit_mean\": 1.02,\n      \"c_pct_misfit\": 9.1,\n      \"lz_c_n_rank_corr\": 0.72,\n      \"emri_c_n_rank_corr\": 0.68,\n      \"pct_agreement_flagged\": 78.3\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table S6: Facet Fit Statistics\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Facet\",\n          \"N\",\n          \"Infit_MNSQ_mean\",\n          \"Infit_MNSQ_range\",\n          \"Outfit_MNSQ_mean\",\n          \"Pct_misfit\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"θ (ability)\",\n            22,\n            1.01,\n            \"0.78–1.25\",\n            1.03,\n            4.5\n          ],\n          [\n            \"b (difficulty)\",\n            580,\n            1.0,\n            \"0.65–1.42\",\n            1.02,\n            5.2\n          ],\n          [\n            \"d (severity)\",\n            8,\n            0.98,\n            \"0.82–1.18\",\n            0.99,\n            0.0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"c (contamination)\",\n            22,\n            1.02,\n            \"0.74–1.38\",\n            1.05,\n            9.1\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table S7: Person-Fit vs c_n Convergent Validity\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Metric\",\n          \"Rank_corr_with_c_n\",\n          \"p_value\",\n          \"Pct_overlap_flagged\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"lz (person-fit)\",\n            0.72,\n            0.0002,\n            78.3\n          ],\n          [\n            \"EMRi (extended)\",\n            0.68,\n            0.0008,\n            73.9\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"整体拟合质量支撑 framework claim：G-MFRM 不是 overfitting 噪声， 而是合理捕捉了数据结构。c_n 的 9.1% misfit 率可在 Limitations 中坦诚报告， 并指向 rank-k extension 的 future work。person-fit/c_n 的 convergent validity (r=0.72) 是 DG-IRT 迁移成功的额外证据。\\n\\n\\nbest 档下 MFRM 拟合良好：θ 和 d 的 infit/outfit 接近 1.0，misfit 率低。 b (items) 的 misfit 略高（5.2%），因为部分 Arena-Hard items 的难度在 不同 judges 间变异大（某些 items 对某些 judges \\\"特别难评\\\"）。 c_n 的 misfit 率最高（9.1%=2/22 models），因为 rank-1 c_n·e_i 假设 对极端模型（极高或极低污染）拟合不完美——这正是论文中坦诚讨论 rank-1 局限性的位置。 lz 和 c_n 的 rank correlation 0.72 表明传统 person-fit 指标确实能部分捕捉 contamination（因为 contaminated models 在高曝光 items 上表现异常好）， 但 c_n 提供了更结构化的解释。两者 78.3% 的重叠验证了 construct coherence。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"confounding_formal_proposition\",\n    \"description\": \"推导 sequential estimator 在 d_j/c_n·e_i 非正交条件下的一阶 bias 近似。 形式化为 Proposition 1（Section 2）。Monte Carlo 验证 bias 近似精度。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"proposition_statement\": \"Under non-orthogonality (Cov(d_j, c_n·e_i) ≠ 0), the bias-first sequential estimator θ̂_seq has first-order bias E[θ̂_seq - θ] ≈ γ·Cov(d_j, c_n·e_i)/Var(d_j) where γ is the contamination gating coefficient. Direction: positive covariance → overestimation of high-contamination models.\\n\",\n      \"mc_n_simulations\": 5000,\n      \"mc_parameter_grid_size\": 50,\n      \"bias_approximation_r2\": 0.94,\n      \"bias_direction_correct_pct\": 97.8,\n      \"max_bias_at_rho_0_6\": 0.31,\n      \"bias_at_rho_0_3\": 0.14,\n      \"real_data_rho\": 0.37,\n      \"real_data_predicted_bias\": 0.17,\n      \"real_data_observed_bias\": 0.19,\n      \"prediction_error_pct\": 10.5\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table S8: Monte Carlo Validation of Bias Approximation\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"rho_range\",\n          \"N_sims\",\n          \"Mean_true_bias\",\n          \"Mean_approx_bias\",\n          \"Approx_R2\",\n          \"Direction_accuracy_pct\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"[-0.8, -0.4]\",\n            1000,\n            -0.28,\n            -0.26,\n            0.93,\n            98.2\n          ],\n          [\n            \"[-0.4, 0.0]\",\n            1000,\n            -0.09,\n            -0.08,\n            0.95,\n            97.5\n          ],\n          [\n            \"[0.0, 0.4]\",\n            1000,\n            0.1,\n            0.09,\n            0.94,\n            97.8\n          ],\n          [\n            \"[0.4, 0.8]\",\n            1000,\n            0.32,\n            0.3,\n            0.93,\n            97.6\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Overall\",\n            5000,\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\",\n            0.94,\n            97.8\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Proposition 1 将 confounding claim 从实证观察提升为理论结果， MC 验证确认近似在实际参数范围内高精度（R²=0.94）。 real data 上 predicted vs observed bias 的一致性（10.5% error） 提供了 \\\"theory predicts, data confirms\\\" 的强叙事弧线。 Section 2 可以先展示 proposition，再用 exp-003 的 bias scatter 作为实证验证。\\n\\n\\n一阶 bias 近似基于 omitted variable bias 的经典结果（Angrist & Pischke 框架 在 psychometric context 的适配）。R²=0.94 表明一阶近似在实际参数范围内精度高。 关键洞察：bias 方向由 Cov(d_j, c_n·e_i) 决定——当严格 judges（高 d_j） 与高污染模型×高曝光 items 的交互为正时，sequential 高估高污染模型。 真实数据 ρ=0.37 > 0 预测正向 bias 0.17 std units，观测值 0.19 std units， 预测误差仅 10.5%——形式化命题在真实数据上得到量化验证。 这为 Section 2 提供了理论 + 实证双重论证。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"wildbench_replication\",\n    \"description\": \"在 WildBench 上复制 G-MFRM pipeline：收集 8 judges × 22 models 评分， ConStat exposure estimation，三阶段拟合，baseline 比较。 验证跨 benchmark 泛化性。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"wildbench_n_items\": 1024,\n      \"kendall_tau_gmfrm_wildbench\": 0.89,\n      \"kendall_tau_sequential_wildbench\": 0.84,\n      \"kendall_tau_uda_wildbench\": 0.85,\n      \"delta_tau_vs_best_baseline_wildbench\": 0.04,\n      \"wilcoxon_p_gmfrm_vs_seq_wildbench\": 0.00021,\n      \"c_n_mean_wildbench\": 0.95,\n      \"c_n_rank_corr_cross_benchmark\": 0.82,\n      \"convergence_max_rhat_wildbench\": 1.02,\n      \"convergence_min_ess_wildbench\": 278\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 5: Cross-Benchmark Replication (WildBench)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Method\",\n          \"WildBench_τ\",\n          \"MT-Bench_τ\",\n          \"Arena-Hard_τ\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Raw Average\",\n            0.8,\n            0.8,\n            0.83\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Sequential\",\n            0.84,\n            0.84,\n            0.86\n          ],\n          [\n            \"UDA\",\n            0.85,\n            0.85,\n            0.87\n          ],\n          [\n            \"**G-MFRM**\",\n            \"**0.89**\",\n            \"**0.90**\",\n            \"**0.91**\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"跨 benchmark 泛化成功：G-MFRM 在第三个独立 benchmark 上同样显著优于全部 baselines。 c_n 跨 benchmark 一致性（r=0.82）是论文的加分项—— 说明 contamination susceptibility 是模型的稳定属性，G-MFRM 估计的不是 benchmark-specific 噪声。\\n\\n\\nWildBench τ=0.89 略低于 MT-Bench+Arena-Hard 的 0.91， 因为 WildBench items 更 open-ended、scoring 更主观， 引入了 G-MFRM 无法完全捕捉的 noise。但仍显著优于全部 baselines（Δτ=0.04）。 c_n_mean=0.95 略低于主数据集的 1.18，因为 WildBench 较新（2024）， 部分 items 未被充分泄漏。跨 benchmark c_n rank correlation 0.82 表明 contamination 是模型属性（不是 benchmark 属性）， 支撑 c_n 作为 meaningful latent trait 的解读。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"adversarial_robustness\",\n    \"description\": \"模拟 Wang et al. (ICLR 2026) 的 adversarial contamination 场景： 对 target model 注入 benchmark items（0%, 5%, 10%, 20% training data）， 测试 G-MFRM c_n 估计是否正确反映注入量， 以及 θ 估计是否对 adversarial contamination 鲁棒。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"c_n_at_0pct_injection\": 0.15,\n      \"c_n_at_5pct_injection\": 0.82,\n      \"c_n_at_10pct_injection\": 1.45,\n      \"c_n_at_20pct_injection\": 2.18,\n      \"c_n_injection_correlation\": 0.97,\n      \"theta_bias_at_0pct\": 0.02,\n      \"theta_bias_at_5pct\": 0.05,\n      \"theta_bias_at_10pct\": 0.08,\n      \"theta_bias_at_20pct\": 0.14,\n      \"theta_bias_sequential_at_20pct\": 0.52,\n      \"robustness_ratio_20pct\": 3.71,\n      \"auc_detecting_contaminated\": 0.94\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table S9: Adversarial Robustness — θ Bias Under Controlled Contamination\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Injection_pct\",\n          \"G-MFRM_c_n\",\n          \"G-MFRM_θ_bias\",\n          \"Sequential_θ_bias\",\n          \"Robustness_ratio\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            0,\n            0.15,\n            0.02,\n            0.03,\n            1.5\n          ],\n          [\n            5,\n            0.82,\n            0.05,\n            0.18,\n            3.6\n          ],\n          [\n            10,\n            1.45,\n            0.08,\n            0.34,\n            4.25\n          ],\n          [\n            20,\n            2.18,\n            0.14,\n            0.52,\n            3.71\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Adversarial robustness 是 reviewer concern 的预防性回应。 G-MFRM 在极端场景（20% injection）下 θ bias 仅为 sequential 的 1/4， 且 c_n 可作为 post-hoc contamination audit 工具（AUC=0.94）。 这将 G-MFRM 从 \\\"evaluation correction method\\\" 提升为 \\\"contamination-aware evaluation framework\\\"。\\n\\nG-MFRM 的 gating mechanism 设计上就是为了 absorb contamination effect into c_n， 所以 c_n 与 injection rate 高度相关（r=0.97）是预期中的。 θ bias 在 20% injection 时仅 0.14（vs sequential 的 0.52）， 因为 G-MFRM 将 contamination inflation 归因于 c_n 而非 θ。 robustness ratio 3.71× 意味着 G-MFRM 的 θ 偏差仅为 sequential 的 27%。 AUC=0.94 表明 c_n 可以作为 contamination detection 工具， 这为论文的 practical impact 增加了一个维度。 注意：这是在 controlled setting（已知注入量）的 validation， 与真实场景的 unknown contamination 有区别，需在论文中说明。\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":1066,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1066}}}
